{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click","id":112231,"title":"Werewolf as a Roleplay Game (making it click)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-13T14:16:04-07:00","id":112231,"title":"Werewolf as a Roleplay Game (making it click)","content":"As the first point of order I\u2019d like to apologise about the length of this post, it\u2019s a bloody essay. Still context is all important in regards to the point I\u2019m trying to get across.<br /> <br /> So, Werewolf as a roleplay game in the WoD (both classic and new). I don\u2019t quite get it. At the same time, I know there is SOMETHING in this game that keeps me wanting to try and get it. Its kinda like a chipped nail or tooth, I can\u2019t help but get snagged on it every time I\u2019m reminded about it.<br /> <br /> This feeling I get about the game I think is partially due to the general like I have for the WoD. The NWoD has not got a single game I dislike. I have issues with several of the lines (Werewolf, Changeling, Mage) and God knows I have my favourites (Vampire, Promethean, Mummy, Demon) but I don\u2019t actively dislike any of them.<br /> <br /> To focus this in a bit more on Werewolf I need to run through some contextual stuff about my history with the concept of a game about Werewolves:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Werewolf the Apocalypse:</b></u><br /> <br /> So I started playing WoD games back in about 2004 on and off. Back then I was neck deep in Masquerade stuff. Found a ST that had been playing Masquerade since it started in the early 90\u2019s. He likewise was basically pure Masquerade focused and was frankly disparaging of a lot of the other Classic World of Darkness game lines.<br /> <br /> I think we are all shaped to a certain extent by our first ST in a system and game line. We grow beyond those initial views as we grow older, but in general they stick with us on some level. I certainly think this is true in my case on at least some level.<br /> <br /> So in general this ST had little time for the other lines in the Classic World of Darkness past Masquerade. He liked bits of Mage, which is why I think I still have a curiosity about Ascension (only recently indulged during the M20 Kickstarter) and he liked bits of Demon the Fallen. Other than that he was pretty scornful of Wraith, Changeling (especially Changeling) and Mummy. Weirdly he gave Kindred of the East a sorta free pass, likely because it was a Masquerade add-on.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he liked exactly one thing about Apocalypse, which was the whole Wyld, Wyver, Wyrm thing. So that bit of fluff came up in his games sometimes. Apart from that, he openly disliked the game. I was kinda indifferent about it and never really read up on it. Till this day I still giggle whenever anyone mentions Weresharks. I kinda give the weirder stuff a free pass as Classic World of Darkness was pretty \u201cout-there\u201d in some ways anyway.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the whole general theme of \u201craging\u201d against something just seemed kinda\u2026immature to me (in the \u201cOh so mature mindset\u201d of a 16 year old). Likewise, the whole \u201ceco-warrior\u201d vibe fell flat. I suspect having an ST talking about <i>\u201cfurry superhero wolf-men\u201d</i> did not help. In general on that note, I have nothing against the furry subculture, but for a long time I had the Werewolf games painted as pretty much pandering to that subculture. Obviously I see in hindsight how irrational such an idea is, but it\u2019s something I honestly believed for a few years.<br /> This is the background I came from going into the NWoD.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Werewolf the Forsaken:</b></u><br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly given my RP background I kinda missed Forsaken for a long time.<br /> <br /> I did not even look at the NWoD (another thing my old ST was very negative about) until 2007. I got Requiem and was one of the few people who instantly liked it. Likewise, by this time I\u2019d moved and met a whole new group of roleplayers. I got clued onto Mage the Awakening when an ST I know ran a year- long campaign I joined from the start.<br /> <br /> Still Werewolf was kinda non-entity for me. They were creatures to keep Vampires in cities and give Spirit Mages a hard time that was about it.<br /> <br /> Finally in 2010 I pick up the Forsaken book, largely as procrastination at the time to avoid working on my research degree. Finally some front line exposure to Werewolf, no more second-hand knowledge or other peoples opinion colouring my intake.<br /> <br /> I found it bland, like <i>\u201cdry white toast\u201d</i> bland (and I\u2019m a guy that found a lot of flavour in the 1.0 version of Requiem, that most people write off for being \u201cbland\u201d). After I got over the initial \u201cnew game\u201d shine (and god do I fall to the \u201cnew game\u201d shine often) I found the game instantly forgettable. Certain aspects appealed to me sure, the Mother Luna stuff fluff was all really interesting. I could take or leave the whole \u201cfather wolf on prehistoric earth\u201d thing, but the Moon related stuff was interesting. The Hosts were interesting antagonists.<br /> <br /> Other stuff, I just did not get.<br /> <br /> Sure there are large Spiritual entities at their foundation but the Tribes being global institutions? Really? Honestly the idea of a large scale &quot;structure&quot; of Werewolves just does not in general work for me. I think it makes sense for Vampires, its got a precedent in fiction if nothing else. I can't recall any stories about multi-millionaire sauv\u00e9 businessmen that are Werewolves, I can think of at least three that are Vampires. For me Werewolves are inherently a symbol of something so primal and chaotic that trying to apply a structure (beyond pack at least) to such a thing inherently damages its thematic resonance.<br /> <br /> Gifts struck me as well\u2026odd. Half the things they do I\u2019ve seen basically no evidence for in pre-existing Werewolf mythology. In comparison to say Requiem were the core Disciplines are all pretty much doing something that Vampires do in mythology or fiction. Honestly, some of the power just seemed kinda present because they could be, I did not feel they added anything to the theme or tone of &quot;Werewolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> In general though, overall assessment was bland. I read a couple of the splat books on and off and that was about it.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Idigam Chronicles:</b></u><br /> <br /> So when this got announced I was less then amazed. The Idigam were one of the less interesting parts of the Werewolf splat fluff that game out. The general idea of Luna\u2019s mutant babies that got banished to the moon and hitched a ride back with Neil Armstrong did not really excite me. Likewise, when mentioned to my local roleplay group we all came the conclusion of Werewolves fighting Idigam on the dark side of the moon <b>IN SPACE</b>! (I blame the third Transformers movie).<br /> <br /> Likewise, I\u2019d moved again in the time between reading the old Forsaken core and the announcement of the Idigam Chronicles. So my local roleplay group had changed again. These guys had actually played about two separate long running Forsaken games in a LARP system. They\u2019d had a mixed bag of experiences and come away a little negative about the game so say the least.<br /> <br /> They found it all a bit to \u201chack and slash\u201d for WoD and the idea of 9/10 feet tall wolf people slinging around great swords was a little too weird for them in the context of NWoD (our world darkly). Likewise, the general complaint that Werewolf is not really a game about Werewolves, but Shaman spirit cops has been voiced. Not to mention that old Harmony was a little too similar to the \u201cpath of do what I want\u201d morally for some of them. Plus their ST was kinda blunt with his Spirit plot, meaning Spirit plot in general is kinda looked down upon as &quot;lazy&quot; or &quot;polarizing&quot; (either you can deal with Spirits or you can't and if you can't Spirit plot is not much fun) in our group. <br /> <br /> To be fair I personally hold issue with how in tune with traditional Werewolf themes Forsaken is and how much \u201cWerewolf\u201d is in Forsaken as is. It seems to miss the anger/control issues (yes I know the game makes an effort in this regard, but I never felt it got the theme across adiquately) and body issues that are inherent underpinnings of the myth. Plus the idea of a fundamentally &quot;primitive&quot; or &quot;primordial&quot; acting out within a modern ordered civilization. Did not feel any of these themes were particularly present or resonant in Forsaken.<br /> <br /> However, the previews start five weeks back and I decide to kill some time reading the articles. The first one does nothing for me beyond giving me an idea of a stronger central tone to the game. Basically the same move Blood and Smoke made for Vampire. Then the Harmony article happened and I got interested. Wolf-Blooded happened and I was impressed at that tonal shift and base alteration. Packs this week gave me hope that whole Totem thing would not such a baseline mechanical process (not to mention about as interesting as Wallpaper paste drying).<br /> So yeah, despite all my misgivings and bad-experiences by proxy it\u2019s got me interested.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Point:</b></u><br /> <br /> With all that history out of the way I can finally come to the point of this post/thread.<br /> <br /> Namely that considering how \u201cother\u201d Werewolf has as a game been throughout both its runs to me as a player and ST I am what other people find so appealing, good, right and loveable about the game?<br /> <br /> What is it about this game that makes it \u201cclick\u201d for you?<br /> <br /> More over what is it about the Idigam Chronicles (despite the limited information we have) that gives you hope that the game will continue to \u201cwork for\u201d you?<br /> <br /> Basically I\u2019m curious to see what point\u2019s people pull out in regards to their thoughts and experiences with the game. As I\u2019m sure there will be many that have never occurred to me.<br /> <br /> The closest someone's ever come to putting a different spin on Werewolf for me is looking at it through stories that having nothing to do with Werewolves. One person suggested looking at Tv shows like Sons or Anarchy or the Walking Dead and look at the groups there as &quot;packs&quot;. I kinda got it better from that point of view. Only the regard to placing an emphasis in Werewolf on &quot;In groups&quot; and &quot;out-groups&quot;. Though without the motorcycle gang motif (which I find a tired and dull sterotype) or zombies (though I do think Werewolf works excellently as a post-apocalyptic game, arguably better then a &quot;modern&quot; game).<br /> <br /> Thanks beforehand for taking the time to read this and reply.<br /> <br /> Hawthorn","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 04-13-2014, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T14:48:54-07:00","id":112247,"title":"","content":"Forsaken 'clicks' to me for few reasons, namely how much it is about the wolves and the pack. Unlike in WtA, Forsaken packs are all the society the Uratha have, and at best their goverments are agreements between packs of a certain city.<br /> <br /> Because there is no larger goverment or society looming over the Uratha, the packs essentially make their own rules and traditions, and build their own survival together. Uratha are not Warriors of anything, they are hunters and survialists. And all this really fits the stronger emphasis on the 'wolf' in the game than in Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T16:08:14-07:00","id":112296,"title":"","content":"First of all, let me applaud this thread, because I think your experiences sum up a lot of people's feelings on the game, myself included. Personally, how I managed to make Forsaken lick for myself was to change the way I play it. (I've never ST'd Forsaken, because I know I wouldn't do the game justice). The only way I can enjoy playing forsaken is by playing a character who experiences her first change either in play, or very recently in her background. For me, it's not a werewolf game if my character does not have to struggle against her wolf nature. It is then placed on the experienced Uratha (who can be PCs, NPC's, or a combination if both) to teach my character that fighting her nature will cause it to fight back even harder against her, and the only way to reach live in Harmony with her self is to embrace what she is, with all it entails (which includes the spirit stuff). I enjoy playing out that inner struggle, eventually resolving it (usually somewhere around the climax of the Story or Chronicle), and ending her character development arc by finally becoming comfortable with it. At that point, when the character has become like the protagonists as described in the books, I tend to lose interest, so I generally plan for that to coincide with the end of the Story or Chronicle.<br /> <br /> What gives me hope for the Idigam Chronicle is that from what I've seen, my personal play-style is going to be actively accommodated instead of being something I have to force to a degree. In fact, I have liked what I've seen in the development blogs, particularly of Harmony and Packs, that I am seriously considering STing a game of it for the first time for my group. I think the Idigam Chronicle is finally going to give me the tools to actually tell the kind of werewolf story I want to tell. It will be a very different take on Forsaken than any of the games I've played in, but I believe it will still be recognizable as Forsaken, spirit action and all. I can only hope as more details are revealed, the direction continues to evoke that feeling for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T16:35:55-07:00","id":112316,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click#post112231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it about this game that makes it \u201cclick\u201d for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>That you can use it as a tool kit if you don't like everything about the setting. At this point our game resembles a promethean as my group has gutted the thing and stapled parts from other games onto it. [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click#post112231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More over what is it about the Idigam Chronicles (despite the limited information we have) that gives you hope that the game will continue to \u201cwork for\u201d you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrase the wolf must hunt. Seems like they are going to put the wolf back into werewolf. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T17:17:00-07:00","id":112333,"title":"","content":"I suppose three things made it click for me. First was the spirit world. As a fan of psychological horror and alien, but not necessarily evil, landscapes, the idea that the scene of a murder can taint the surrounding area for decades, that something as simple as a new store opening can have a wild series of consequences, and someone walking into a room and staying there until they die because it's a waiting room (gone wrong) all appeal to me, and the Werewolves have the closest connection to the spirit, coming from it and all. Second, the enemies. Such a wide and varied bunch, from moral ambiguity to out and out malevolence, from people exactly like you (pure) to twisted versions of yourself (shartha, claimed) and everything else, just greatly appealing. And lastly, the instinct and passion. Werewolves aren't all immortals who have to be parasites off humanity. From the moment of your first change, you're full of great urges and senses, and from there you can really do whatever you want. You can throw yourself into humanity, being a leader of men and women and an exemplar of your kind, or use your powers over the spirit to hedge things your own way in other paths (the criminal or business sectors, or others). Or you could just toss it all away and romp around in the spirit like a big alpha monster. You can be brothers with your packmates, or a loner willing to help occasionally.<br /> <br /> The only real draw for me for the Idigam Chronicles so far is the fixed up mechanics, which were really scattershot in Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> I never really cared how accurate to the life of a wolf the game was, or to some iconic werewolf movie, but having been on the boards a while I see a lot of people apparently really care a lot about it. So if it gets them more into the game, that's great, since popularity will likely equate to more profits and, thus, more books.<br /> <br /> Personally if they were going to change the fluff I would have preferred an official Wolves of Outer Darkness, but they seem to be sticking mostly to Forsaken's setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2014, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T19:33:22-07:00","id":112383,"title":"","content":"Let me state explicitly what Apocalypse is about. It's about watching the world in it's final days and knowing it. Knowing that you are to blame for this, you and the generations before it. It's about lamenting that which hasn't been lost yet. Knowing that you were born too late to do anything to stop the inevitable demise of everything. When the Garou first changed, they go thru denial and isolation. Then they can quickly set into a long stage of rage, rage at the state of the world, at the responsibilities you have to shoulder, at your enemies. The bargaining step comes from the glimmer of hope for a new tomorrow, the many quest the last packs undertake in a last ditch attempt at saving the dying world. The Garou have a word for the next step: Harano - not unlike depression. But if they ever reach the last step? acceptance, they have been likely corrupted beyond redemption.<br /> <br /> Forsaken isn't about that. Forsaken is about something more personal. Your turf, your friends, your family, and trying to balance your primal essence with a glimmer of humanity, because if you don't... who will?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T22:30:56-07:00","id":112430,"title":"","content":"&quot;You? Hunt us? Arrogant mongrels! You are too few; we are legions. You must be born to the flesh; we take the flesh at our whim. O you wolves howl your fear to the uncaring moon, for she has given you up to us!&quot;<br /> <br /> The world is in shadow. To one side stretches the forest, to the other the city. Your claws are stained with blood. Your senses whisper of prey that runs before you, and of predators who stalk even the likes of you. You hear the howls of your brothers and sisters. Luna rises. Your blood boils. It is time to hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> The world hates you. This isn't a figurative thing - the world doesn't acknowledge your innate right to exist. You're a half-flesh half-spirit abomination that shouldn't be. Shadowy entities hate and hunt you because you're what keeps them from building their own little hell-kingdoms in the world of man. Spiders and rats dig into people's brain and hearts, controlling them the way people drive cars. Wolves stalk your children and friends because of some sin your ancestors committed thousands of years and at least one apocalypse ago. People fear you, and would hate you if they knew what you are, if they knew you sometimes look at them and can't help thinking &quot;food&quot;.<br /> <br /> The world hates you, and does everything it can to kill you.<br /> <br /> Doesn't that make you angry?<br /> <br /> Show them how strong the Forsaken are. It is time to hunt. <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> I'll try and summarize what I like best about Werewolf.<br /> <br /> First, Werewolf allows you to play heroes. This is what the Forsaken can be in your game. They're making a last stand against the countless enemies of the Forsaken, sacrificing their own future so that their loved ones can live free from physical harm or spiritual incursions. You can't win, but your efforts could mean that the people you love will live, for just one other day. That's powerful.<br /> <br /> Secondly, Werewolf allows you to play monsters. As I said, werewolves are empowered, but they aren't always in control of their powers. A Forsaken can lose his temper, tearing enemies and innocents equally apart. Sooner or later, this will happen in every werewolf's life. Some werewolves might feel guilty about it. Others don't have the necessary compassion. When werewolves fall from grace, they fall hard.<br /> <br /> The spirituality of Werewolf is also a selling point: It's awfully potent for a werewolf pack to be questing through invisible realms in which symbols and hidden meaning are more important than substance. The Shadow is a great source for wisdom, exploration and adventure as much as it is a source of Lovecraftian horrors and darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>The antagonists</b>: Spiders that enter the human body via orifices, eat your brain and move your body around the way people drive cars. Spiritual manifestations of your own deepest fears and passions. Cunning, sly spirit beings hiding in the souls of your friends and loved ones, corrupting their minds and bodies from the inside. Raging fanatics in werewolf skin who want you dead because they can't overcome their own moral failings. Demon-gods from an age gone by.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want to run Werewolf. In fact, I'm currently planning a Werewolf game set in Kosovo in 2008. I want to play a game about a pack that is internally divided at times, sometimes even to the point that blood is spilled and bones are broken and things that cannot ever be unsaid are said, while, when worst comes to worst, still keeping together and cooperating and operating in synergy like only a true pack of wolves can do. I want there to be a Rahu protagonists who is, at times, really fucking scared about being born and chosen to kill and slash and maim, while, on some level, accepting it as part of his destiny. I want there to be a PC whose loss of something precious to him defines much of his being, and is hurting, sometimes to the point that discarding his current life and going Bale Hound or Predator King seems like the only sensible choice to him, if it wasn't for his packmates. I want individual packmates to actively devote their lives to emulating the wolf-gods of yore. I want the pack to hunt with a pack totem, a being of the Spirit Wilds that will always be distant from the pack in that it's this unknowable spirit being that does not and cannot understand many of the concepts known to the minds of people, while at the same time grudgingly respecting the pack because of the blood they have shed together fighting on the same side.<br /> <br /> And, hey, in case I haven't made it completely obvious, the player characters are monsters. Some by choice, some because they can't help themselves. This is a part of their nature that cannot be changed. The most peaceful, loving Uratha can turn into ten feets of raging wolf-death, and she might not be able to stop herself from doing so if circumstances are wrong. Werewolves feel nervous and claustrophobic in their human form (the sheep's skin) because that's where their strong natural senses and powers are denied to them. This is something that affects them all the time. They get angry easily - and it's not anger, it's wrath. We all occasionally feel like hitting someone. Well, in the case of the Forsaken, they feel like tearing someone's head off, and it's something they totally can and will do if pushed to it. And it's not just their terrible wrath, it's also the fact that they're literally higher on the food chain than us. You wake up next to your girlfriend in the morning, and she's still sleeping and looks so sweet and you just can't stop your instincts from telling you to think &quot;food&quot;. There is nothing that tastes better to a werewolf than human. This is you (the PC you), everyday. It gets worse. You do things that upset the fragile balance between human, wolf and spirit, you start exhibiting traits of behaviour associated with movie wolves. Maybe you're in permanent Death Rage all full moon. Maybe you can't stop yourself from collecting the fingers of strangers. Werewolf can fall from grace, and they fall hard.<br /> <br /> I want the pack to have human relatives, friends and foibles. I want the protagonists to have moments in which they feel innately superior to those weaker, fragile beings who're so very foolish and ignorant about the truths of the World of Darkness. I want them to be, at other times, jealous of humans, of being able to blend in with society, of not being burdened with the Hunt, of not knowing. At the same time, I want the characters to live in fear of what might happen to their loved ones if they lose control or if some part of the darkness decides to target those. (Innocent) people should have terrible things happening to them, too, seeing as this is a horror game. People die. They get turned crazy by spirits. They find themselves receptacles for spirits in their brain or rats eating their hearts.<br /> <br /> What I also want is the game to feature packs of Pure werewolves who are, on some level, the same kind of dudes and girls as the protagonists, only that they have been put into an invariably different position by fate. I want the Pure to be this implacable antagonist that cannot be argued with. They come only to spout propaganda, hurt your loved ones, kill you and/or oppose everything the protagonists are fighting for. I want the Pure to be utterly merciless in their actions, because mercy is not something that can ever have a place in their society.<br /> <br /> There should be spirit antagonists in the game. Many of them should have sprung into being based on the dreams, wishes, aspirations and fears of humans and werewolves, including the pack. Spirit encounters are never random. You don't get to face some anger spirit, you'll face the embodied wrath of a teenager about to go on a killing spree in his school. The murder spirit trying to rip your guts out is an idealized reflection of that serial killer who slaughtered a two digit number of people in the city decades ago. The lust spirit trying to seduce you - it's your own repressed sexuality, trying to find a release.<br /> <br /> I want there to be things like a school haunted by the embodied (in the spirit sense) Fear of that teacher who once raped and murdered a student, or a dude who is so overwhelmed by Wrath possessing him that he cannot see any course of action other than what the spirit possessing him tells him to do. There should be tangible spirits of Apathy haunting homes for the elderly. Some of these spirits can and should only be fought by venturing into the nightmare of that other world and sticking your claws into them until they stop moving. Others might require the Ithaeur of the pack investigating the innate rules and laws govering spirits. And others might be exorcized by little more than the right words to their host.<br /> <br /> It's not a proper Werewolf game if it doesn't have rats squirming around in remote, hidden places, trying to open pandora's box and let their diseases reign free in the world. There should also be a place for spiders hiding behind people's eyes, taking on the packmates individually, using fire and poison and silver. And there should be a Cahalith of the pack having nightmares about that Pangaean demon-god, the one trapped below the earth aeons ago, arising to take its place.<br /> <br /> That's Werewolf: the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T23:18:14-07:00","id":112446,"title":"","content":"As a setting, and as fluff werewolf has always clicked with me. As an actual game...Ehhh, get back to me once the Idigam Chronicles are out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:52:47-07:00","id":112637,"title":"","content":"I want to be clear that this is all just my personal opinion, and is not anything &quot;official&quot; (I'm still new, I don't think they'd let me do anything official yet) or anything of the sort. I will cheat a little on the one question, but I'll call that out. Still, this is all just my personal view and opinion. Disclaimer out of the way, here we go...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click#post112231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it about this game that makes it \u201cclick\u201d for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The game clicked for me from the outset, actually. I was a big <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> fan, so of course I was excited to see what the &quot;new&quot; Werewolf game would be like. I saw the teasers for the game, and immediately fell in love with the Hunters in Darkness. An entire tribe that embodies the scary predator in the shadows? Yes, please!<br /> <br /> For me, and how I was at the time (and continue to be), Forsaken just fit more of what I was looking for in a game about werewolves. I was less interested in the grand, cosmic scale that Apocalypse has, and more interested in the personal stories. What makes these werewolves tick? Why do they do what they do? That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click#post112231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More over what is it about the Idigam Chronicles (despite the limited information we have) that gives you hope that the game will continue to \u201cwork for\u201d you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where I'm both cheating a bit, and must answer in vagaries to avoid spoilers.<br /> <br /> I think the setting has continued to be scary. I just got to read some tribal write ups yesterday, and the Hunters scare the shit out of me. So of course I want to play one. Er, again. For the third time. (What can I say, I like the Meninna!) The mechanics are, I think, much tighter. Chris did an excellent job with the Gifts, for instance. I'll admit I'm a bit biased because I wrote a chunk of it (or am writing, would be more appropriate to say as we're not at final drafts yet). But I'll stand by my statements.<br /> <br /> As much as I already loved <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b>, I am actively chomping at the bit to playtest this thing. Any game that makes me want to play it is a good thing. A game that I already love making me want to play it more? I'm sold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click#post112231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I\u2019m curious to see what point\u2019s people pull out in regards to their thoughts and experiences with the game. As I\u2019m sure there will be many that have never occurred to me.<br /> <br /> The closest someone's ever come to putting a different spin on Werewolf for me is looking at it through stories that having nothing to do with Werewolves. One person suggested looking at Tv shows like Sons or Anarchy or the Walking Dead and look at the groups there as &quot;packs&quot;. I kinda got it better from that point of view. Only the regard to placing an emphasis in Werewolf on &quot;In groups&quot; and &quot;out-groups&quot;. Though without the motorcycle gang motif (which I find a tired and dull sterotype) or zombies (though I do think Werewolf works excellently as a post-apocalyptic game, arguably better then a &quot;modern&quot; game).</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing here is that Forsaken is very much &quot;Us&quot; and &quot;Them.&quot; The pack is the &quot;us&quot; part, and everyone else? &quot;Them.&quot; <br /> <br /> For instance, I have a lot of friends, but I have one group of friends where we just click with one another. We have our in-jokes and so forth, and we say things to one another that, when we say them, they're funny. Everyone knows that nobody really means those things. Especially because, if someone outside of our group said those things, any one of us would be all over that person in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> That's a pack. They'll give each other shit all day long. They'll argue. They may even fight (and for the werewolf members of the pack, yeah that may well happen due to Rage). But at the end of the day, no matter what is tearing at them from inside, they'll stand shoulder-to-shoulder against any external threat.<br /> <br /> I like that. While I certainly enjoy Vampire from a &quot;let's be a conniving bastard&quot; angle (that's pretty much my default mode of playing that game), what I like about Werewolf is that, no matter how much the world hates and fears you, you have someone there for you. You have people to watch your back, help defend you, pick you up when you fall, and share in your successes. For me, that's a good thing to have in a game.<br /> <br /> Those are just my thoughts, anyway. Take them for what you will.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T09:19:40-07:00","id":112695,"title":"","content":"I hear a lot of talk of Heros, and glory, and fighting against insurmountable odds because if you don't, who will, and... Absolutely none of that resonates as &quot;werewolf&quot; to me. That's why I've never been able to enjoy playing it as one of the protagonists the books describe. Sure, being that doomed hero can be fun, but when I want that, I play Hunter. When I look to werewolf, I want to be a wretched shell of a woman, who has given up everything to protect her loved ones; not from some alien threat from the shadow world, but from the monster she becomes when the moon is right. I don't want to be afraid of the evil spirits that are out there, I want to be afraid of the wild beast inside myself. That's the biggest problem with werewolf for me, is that werewolf has the potential to be the best personal horror game in the entire World of Darkness, and it choses instead to focus on external horror. Don't get me wrong, the antagonists are cool, but to me they will never be as scary as the wolf within. And I get that Forsaken has its own identity and the werewolf game I really want would be too far removed from that identity, it would basically be a different game. But if I have to play a super hero, at least let me be Bruce Banner and not Tony Stark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:10:12-07:00","id":112734,"title":"","content":"... luckily, Werewolf is really not a game whose horror is entirely external, or where you play super heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:19:27-07:00","id":112738,"title":"","content":"Its interesting to see not only the responses people have given so far, but the <i>TYPE</i> of response given about Werewolf as a game so far. <br /> <br /> People seem kninda well...passionate about Werewolf. They engage with the emotional statement of the game and view it through that lens. Ephsy, Christian A and Charlaquin all gave very interesting replies seated in an emotional response. Another good example of this is the opening quote on the TvTropes entry for Werewolf the Apocalypse. When people make statements about this game its clear that is <b>means</b> something to them. <br /> <br /> I like that. Its good that people care, that they engage with something on a deeper level. I can also perhaps see why its one of the things I never got about Werewolf. Firstly, as I mentioned I never felt inspired by Werewolf when reading it. Secondly, I guess I'm not the most emotionally driven roleplayer. I fully believe and support the idea that a good PC needs to be emotionally complex and engaged with on an emotional level, however, I think Werewolf involves a peak of emotion I don't usually associate with my roleplay. <br /> <br /> Once again, to go back to other WoD games I enjoy. <br /> <br /> Vampire has a lot of pathos and tragedy in it but I've always seen it as a fundamentally intellectual game. Its about trying to stay rational in the face of the completely chaotic beast inside you to a certain degree (though secondary to the staying human in face of being a monster theme). Its also very much a game of planning and scheming and staying one step ahead of the competition.<br /> <br /> Promethean is about learning to feel almost. Mimicing human responses to things, faking what you feel until its genuine. Its about wondering what empathy is, then why its important and then how its used and for what purpose. Yes Promethean's feel extremes of emotion in Torment and act out on that. I've always rationalized that response in relation to a child acting out at the world that hurt it. For some that's a temper tantrum that breaks their surroundings, for others its spiteful behavior at those that hurt them for others its a detachment from the source of that pain. Basically I can rationalize the emotional extremes involved.<br /> <br /> Mummy like Promethean is a process of discovering emotion. The only difference is that Mummy's are rediscovering their morals, feelings and self while Promethean are building all that from scratch. The journey of Apotheosis is a human journey, one that engages with the emotions of the Mummy in question and makes him examine them, but its got a religious and intellectual element as well.<br /> <br /> Demon, more so then even Vampire, I think is a game about planning and schemes and counter-ploys and cons. Demons can be emotional, despite their absolute ability to hide what they are feeling from outside observation and I like that in many cases emotion is the catalyst for a Demon to fall. However, from reading Demon I never got a particularly &quot;emotional&quot; feel from them, they have the human spectrum of emotion sure, but I felt the emotions at play in Demon are very much a secondary theme to intellectual exercise of staying one step ahead of the God-Machine. <br /> <br /> Anyway, to sum-up that point. I think I engage with roleplay in a more intellectual way then emotional way. As I've mentioned I feel the emotional element is important and has its place, but its not my primary draw. So maybe that's one reason Werewolf has never clicked for me, since it seems to be about well being angry at various thing (yourself, the world) and afraid of various things (yourself, the world). <br /> <br /> The other thing that is brought up a lot by people giving examples is the hero's thing. Charlaquin already brought this up, but to kinda reinforce the point a little. Hero's are fun to play, we all enjoy a good hero's tale. Its not really what I come to the World of Darkness for though. For me the WoD is full of flawed people making the best choices then can given the circumstances they are forced into or find themselves in. Some might be &quot;heroic&quot; in that they try and do the right thing or act as the &quot;white knight&quot; or &quot;moral exemplar&quot; but for me 9 times out of 10 these character end up tarnished by the world and compromising their own morality. Vampire is of course, all about this and I am not saying I want every WoD game to be Vampire. I like that Promethean, for example, can have genuine innocence and naivety in it and can do such a wonderful job of showing what happens when innocence is ripped away from a person. <br /> <br /> Feeding into this is the idea of moral ambiguity. I can see an argument that the Forsaken are not necessarily the &quot;good guys&quot;, I can't really see an argument that any of the antagonists could be seen as the &quot;good guys&quot;. The Pure maybe, in their most moderate form and if you squint slightly. Everything else the Forsaken fight are so inherently evil or alien (or both) that they boarder on being a little 1-note as villains for me. Once again to contrast with other game lines: Vampire has a similar problem, but VII and the Brood can be made sympathetic and legitimate with enough work on the ST's part. Prometheans Pandorans are monsters, but once again their inherently flawed nature can be played up and I found the write up for the Centimentani to be the best of any antagonist group in any of the NWoD game lines. Mummy has the Shaunkhsen who are monstrous but inherently tragic and do have a legitimate moral greavence with the protagonists, the Deceived are possibly more in the &quot;morally right&quot; category then the Arisen. Demon's the odd one out really, Angels are as implacable as Spirits, but a Demon can at least make one fall and Exiles present and interesting &quot;moral grey&quot; and &quot;third path&quot; between the groups. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, the term &quot;heroic&quot; is not something I apply to the idea of a Werewolf in my head. Can a Werewolf do heroic deeds? Maybe. However, the whole idea of &quot;fighting the good fight&quot; or &quot;persevering in the face of sure defeat&quot; or &quot;clinging to the last shred of hope&quot; is more a set of troupes I apply to old heroic saga's like the Norse Myths of Ragnarok or the 300 Spartans against the Persians. Its not something that &quot;clicks&quot; in my mind as associated withe Werewolves in any way. Short of making Viking Werewolves with great axes and then everything gets way, way to weird for me to see any of it happening in the World of Darkness as I imagine it (our world reflected darkly). <br /> <br /> For me Werewolf is about internal control and the lose of control over the self. In this way I see it as a metaphor for body issues really, its about loosing control over your physical self (the changes it inflicts on your body). This is coupled with a fear of madness and the the psychological sense of self (the loss of the rational and moral self to animal instinct). Like Charlaquin has said, Werewolf stories function primarily on internalized horror, where the self becomes the other and is the source of fear (in a modern day sense The Hulk does provide an excellent touchstone for reference). Everything I've read about Apocalypse and Forsaken kinda overlooks what I consider to be a central set of themes in favour of externalizing the horror into Lovecraftian entities from another realm. I kinda find this the largest stumble of Werewolf as a game. <br /> <br /> Now, I can see how a game involving the sort of themes I am talking about could be well...hard to play and frankly not necessarily a lot of fun. So I can see why those have not been emphasized. In general I guess I could do with having a bit of Promethean's themes of isolation and control issues injected into Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:19:44-07:00","id":112740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112734#post112734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... luckily, Werewolf is really not a game whose horror is entirely external, or where you play super heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is contrary both to my experiences playing Werewolf, and several of the reports here of what makes the game click for people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:28:06-07:00","id":112747,"title":"","content":"Didn't see anything about playing superheroes in anyone's post other than that of the first poster; and I'm sure you understand that this is not the way the game is <i>intended </i>to be played.<br /> <br /> When I said<br /> <br /> &quot;First, Werewolf allows you to play heroes. This is what the Forsaken can be in your game. They're making a last stand against the countless enemies of the Forsaken, sacrificing their own future so that their loved ones can live free from physical harm or spiritual incursions. You can't win, but your efforts could mean that the people you love will live, for just one other day. That's powerful.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I mean is, taken in the context of this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Secondly, Werewolf allows you to play monsters. As I said, werewolves are empowered, but they aren't always in control of their powers. A Forsaken can lose his temper, tearing enemies and innocents equally apart. Sooner or later, this will happen in every werewolf's life. Some werewolves might feel guilty about it. Others don't have the necessary compassion. When werewolves fall from grace, they fall hard.&quot;<br /> <br /> , werewolves are heroes in the classical, mythical sense. They aren't heroes because they're lawful good. They're heroes because they do grand, terrible things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:38:52-07:00","id":112754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112738#post112738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, to sum-up that point. I think I engage with roleplay in a more intellectual way then emotional way. As I've mentioned I feel the emotional element is important and has its place, but its not my primary draw. So maybe that's one reason Werewolf has never clicked for me, since it seems to be about well being angry at various thing (yourself, the world) and afraid of various things (yourself, the world).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of a Promethean game that's about the experience of being born and experiencing the world from the point of view of a child; and Mummy, whose narrative focus is old age; Werewolf is about growing up. Werewolf is about puberty.<br /> <br /> There's the coarse analogies - you &quot;change&quot;, you become stronger, hairier, angrier. You have to deal with this newfound strength and also the emotions raging through your body.<br /> <br /> There's the coming of age thing - you are taking over from dad's responsibilities, you are growing up, you are learning what it is to be a man, you are finding your pack, defining your new role in life; Werewolf is also about refusing to take the path of least resistance represented by the choices the Pure and the Bale Hounds make; it's about growing and finding yourself as a person - and the many, many ways this can go wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112738#post112738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing that is brought up a lot by people giving examples is the hero's thing. Charlaquin already brought this up, but to kinda reinforce the point a little. Hero's are fun to play, we all enjoy a good hero's tale. Its not really what I come to the World of Darkness for though. For me the WoD is full of flawed people making the best choices then can given the circumstances they are forced into or find themselves in. Some might be &quot;heroic&quot; in that they try and do the right thing or act as the &quot;white knight&quot; or &quot;moral exemplar&quot; but for me 9 times out of 10 these character end up tarnished by the world and compromising their own morality. Vampire is of course, all about this and I am not saying I want every WoD game to be Vampire. I like that Promethean, for example, can have genuine innocence and naivety in it and can do such a wonderful job of showing what happens when innocence is ripped away from a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are Byronic heroes; they're also heroes in the classical sense. Werewolf takes the more cynical approach to classic heroes, which is that they're kinda jerks, and they fight over pride, and while they accomplish great things, it's just as often &quot;great&quot; as in &quot;great and terrible&quot; than as in &quot;great and good.&quot; Werewolves as classical heroic archetypes includes characters like Achilles and Oddyseus and Beowulf. Hercules killed his wife and kids in a fit of anger, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112738#post112738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I can see how a game involving the sort of themes I am talking about could be well...hard to play and frankly not necessarily a lot of fun. So I can see why those have not been emphasized.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. This is, in fact, the main reason as for why Ethan Skemp chose not to make Werewolf: the Forsaken the same game as Vampire: the Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:40:53-07:00","id":112755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112738#post112738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding into this is the idea of moral ambiguity. I can see an argument that the Forsaken are not necessarily the &quot;good guys&quot;, I can't really see an argument that any of the antagonists could be seen as the &quot;good guys&quot;. The Pure maybe, in their most moderate form and if you squint slightly. Everything else the Forsaken fight are so inherently evil or alien (or both) that they boarder on being a little 1-note as villains for me. Once again to contrast with other game lines: Vampire has a similar problem, but VII and the Brood can be made sympathetic and legitimate with enough work on the ST's part. Prometheans Pandorans are monsters, but once again their inherently flawed nature can be played up and I found the write up for the Centimentani to be the best of any antagonist group in any of the NWoD game lines. Mummy has the Shaunkhsen who are monstrous but inherently tragic and do have a legitimate moral greavence with the protagonists, the Deceived are possibly more in the &quot;morally right&quot; category then the Arisen. Demon's the odd one out really, Angels are as implacable as Spirits, but a Demon can at least make one fall and Exiles present and interesting &quot;moral grey&quot; and &quot;third path&quot; between the groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you haven't read about Bale Hounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:47:41-07:00","id":112758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112747#post112747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't see anything about playing superheroes in anyone's post other than that of the first poster; and I'm sure you understand that this is not the way the game is <i>intended </i>to be played.<br /> <br /> When I said<br /> <br /> &quot;First, Werewolf allows you to play heroes. This is what the Forsaken can be in your game. They're making a last stand against the countless enemies of the Forsaken, sacrificing their own future so that their loved ones can live free from physical harm or spiritual incursions. You can't win, but your efforts could mean that the people you love will live, for just one other day. That's powerful.&quot;<br /> <br /> What I mean is, taken in the context of this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Secondly, Werewolf allows you to play monsters. As I said, werewolves are empowered, but they aren't always in control of their powers. A Forsaken can lose his temper, tearing enemies and innocents equally apart. Sooner or later, this will happen in every werewolf's life. Some werewolves might feel guilty about it. Others don't have the necessary compassion. When werewolves fall from grace, they fall hard.&quot;<br /> <br /> , werewolves are heroes in the classical, mythical sense. They aren't heroes because they're lawful good. They're heroes because they do grand, terrible things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I see what you mean. Apologies, superheroes was a bit of illustrative hyperbole on my part. What I was trying to get at is that there is nothing about &quot;making a last stand against the countless enemies of the Forsaken, sacrificing their own future so that their loved ones can live free from physical harm or spiritual incursions. You can't win, but your efforts could mean that the people you love will live, for just one other day.&quot; that feels even remotely werewolf-like to me, and that's why I have always struggled to enjoy the game. You are absolutely right that it's a powerful story, but it's not the story I want to tell or to take part in when the central characters are werewolves. Like I said, when I want that game, I play Hunter.<br /> <br /> Now, taking your second point that in werewolf you play as monsters, that while you have powers you are not always in control of them, etc. that does resonate as werewolf to me. The problem is, in my experience, that is not focused on enough. It's absolutely there in the game, which is why I've been able to make the game click for myself, by playing characters that play up that aspect of the game and play down the other aspect. But it's the primary reason I've had such difficulty getting into it. For me, personally, there is too much of the former and not enough of the latter. Another part of the problem for me is that in Forsaken, when you are in control, you are still empowered. What's most compelling to me about the concept of werewolves in general is that they're entirely human... right up until they're monsters. Their power and their monstrousness are inextricably linked, they can't have one without the other. Like Bruce Banner and the Hulk, or like Dr. Jeckyl and Mr. Hyde. Forsaken can't deliver that for me, because even when the Uratha aren't monsters, they're still heroes.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I realize the game that I want is too different from the game Forsaken is, and it would be unreasonable to expect it to change into the game I want. But what excites me about Idigam Chronicles is that (from what little we've been shown so far) it is giving me the tools to tell the kind of werewolf story I want to tell, without gutting the game that already exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T10:51:33-07:00","id":112762,"title":"","content":"We told him how it clicked, or didn't, for us. If he's too intellectual for for it, that's him. Not everyone is going to like every game, and if you come at it with the intention of not liking it, nothing's going to change.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's no one here who's enjoyed every game they've ever encountered, so lets cut the guy some slack and let him see things how he wants to see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T11:02:54-07:00","id":112773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112758#post112758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was trying to get at is that there is nothing about &quot;making a last stand against the countless enemies of the Forsaken, sacrificing their own future so that their loved ones can live free from physical harm or spiritual incursions. You can't win, but your efforts could mean that the people you love will live, for just one other day.&quot; that feels even remotely werewolf-like to me, and that's why I have always struggled to enjoy the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally find <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiess_of_Kaltenbrun\" target=\"_blank\">Thiess of Kaltenbrun</a> a plenty compelling long-term gaming prospect, particularly when linked to the imagery of hellhounds, the Wild Hunt, berserkers, primal shamanism, a world that runs on a predatory version of the contagion principle, and the complicated reputation of dogs and wolves as a whole, but to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T11:06:08-07:00","id":112778,"title":"","content":"So, I'm gonna cheat a bit and start with something I posted elsewhere on the Forsaken forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I first picked up <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b>, I thought the experience was going to me much like the one I had with <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>. I expected a lot of what was in <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> to be brought over, but stripped down to archetypes and not stereotypes, and focused on the individual player-character level struggles, not the world-spanning problems. I had very little interest in <b>Apocalypse</b>, but since I've almost spent more time as an ST than as a player, I made sure to always have the corebooks from all the lines in case I was asked to run one of them or introduce elements from that game. So, I bought <b>Forsaken</b> expecting it to collect dust more often than be read.<br /> <br /> What I got was many of the conventions of <b>Apocalypse </b>flipped on its head and instead of fuzzy superheroes, what I was given was Uratha, The People. People with a duty to their family, their tribe (or Tribes) and to their race as a whole. I got a family with one big promise expected of the children - keep up the family tradition. I got a proper respect of the heritage of shape-shifting (it comes from animism, folks, it's that damn old!) and all the old traditions that come with it. I got The People, who understand that the separations between flesh and spirit or animal and man are false and they <i>know it</i> because they can <i>see it</i>. Every day, all around them, right there in front of their eyes. I got the children of Father Wolf and Mother Luna, the Great Hunter and the Queen of Air and Darkness. Gods of the Shadow Realm giving birth to tiny, fleeting lives because <i>they </i>wanted to be part of the cycle of life. Those children being the products of passion and gaining the gifts (and Gifts) of such a heritage. The power of the Wolf, the flexibility of the Moon, the drive to Hunt, and all while being something that's fully human or animal or flesh or spirit, but a balancing force between all those things. Gone were the spirits to continually praised their &quot;oh so worthy protectors&quot; who tried to claim that everything that came after them was &quot;unclean&quot;. Instead I got a Spirit Realm that placed werewolves firmly within the food chain, no better or worse than any other predators, as long as they could hold their own. Also gone were the wolf-men running around in full war form developing elaborate martial arts and complex rituals. The beast-man was now for one thing - kill everything in sight - and like all such weapons, it was dangerous and not something to be toyed with. There were no more Rage traits, just rage. There were no more Great Caerns, just &quot;our territory&quot;. There were no more epic warriors, just The People. <b>People who struggle every day with what they see around them and use what advantages they have to make their little corner of the world better.</b> </div> </div> </div>These were the first few things that drew me into Forsaken and that last statement is bolded for a reason. It's what is the foundation of Forsaken to me. Territory, Tribes, The People....all these terms make it clear to me what their focus is supposed to be - home and family. Threats from without and threats from within are always looming because the Uratha only have so much they can call their own and so many things are trying to take it away from them. Spirits, Ridden, Pure, your own Rage.....all of them could easily bring the entire house of cards down.<br /> <br /> My experiences playing it have been limited (I got to run it, not be a character), but the entire game with the Forsaken was all about that. &quot;I am a monster, but there are worse monsters out there and they can tear my world apart for no other reason for the gits and shiggles.&quot; Yeah, it can be kinda similar to Hunter, but the Uratha <i>are </i>hunters, so of course there will be crossover. The difference is that in Hunter, the monsters are &quot;them&quot;. In Forsaken, the monsters are &quot;us&quot;. Pure and Bale Hounds are Uratha, too. Spirits are &quot;cousins&quot; of a sort. Ridden are another &quot;kin&quot; of sorts as another half-flesh/half-spirit being. The threats can just as easily come from behind the borders of the territory as outside of it. In fact, they are more likely to come from within because the spirits can slip in easily and the Pure and the Bale-Hounds aren't always marked as such. The monster from within is a part of Forsaken not just because of the threats of Rage, but also the threats of family. It's another kind of personal horror. A vampire only has he own unlife to lose, an Uratha has so much more that can be destroyed and still leave him around to suffer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:00:11-07:00","id":112829,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly <b>Awakening</b> ST, but had mixed feelings to <b>Forsaken</b> before, and just like Original Poster, I would like to love this game. But my general point of view is with <b>Charlaquin</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112758#post112758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I see what you mean. Apologies, superheroes was a bit of illustrative hyperbole on my part. What I was trying to get at is that there is nothing about &quot;making a last stand against the countless enemies of the Forsaken, sacrificing their own future so that their loved ones can live free from physical harm or spiritual incursions. You can't win, but your efforts could mean that the people you love will live, for just one other day.&quot; that feels even remotely werewolf-like to me, and that's why I have always struggled to enjoy the game. You are absolutely right that it's a powerful story, but it's not the story I want to tell or to take part in when the central characters are werewolves. Like I said, when I want that game, I play Hunter.<br /> <br /> Now, taking your second point that in werewolf you play as monsters, that while you have powers you are not always in control of them, etc. that does resonate as werewolf to me. The problem is, in my experience, that is not focused on enough. It's absolutely there in the game, which is why I've been able to make the game click for myself, by playing characters that play up that aspect of the game and play down the other aspect. But it's the primary reason I've had such difficulty getting into it. For me, personally, there is too much of the former and not enough of the latter. Another part of the problem for me is that in Forsaken, when you are in control, you are still empowered. What's most compelling to me about the concept of werewolves in general is that they're entirely human... right up until they're monsters. Their power and their monstrousness are inextricably linked, they can't have one without the other. Like Bruce Banner and the Hulk, or like Dr. Jeckyl and Mr. Hyde. Forsaken can't deliver that for me, because even when the Uratha aren't monsters, they're still heroes.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I realize the game that I want is too different from the game Forsaken is, and it would be unreasonable to expect it to change into the game I want. But what excites me about Idigam Chronicles is that (from what little we've been shown so far) it is giving me the tools to tell the kind of werewolf story I want to tell, without gutting the game that already exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bascilly, even if <b>Forsaken</b> is much more werewolf-ish than <b>Apocalypse</b> ever will be, it was still not enought for me to run it. Partially becuase of all Shadow-centrism of game, making all antagosnits about Spirits, not World of Darkness around you. I run one fun game of <b>Chaging Breeds</b> and liked it becuase it wasn't so centered on Shadow, and more on material world and both humans and shapechangers themselves.<br /> <br /> You see, as <b>Mage </b>ST, I see Shadow as dull realm. In <b>Awakening</b> you have material world, dream realm ( Astral Realm ), land of dead ( Underworld ) and many, many more. But's that <b>Mage</b>. The true problem I found animalistic nature of Shadow to be too simple and anoying in running it. I even don't like to run it in my <b>Mage </b>games. Compared to <b>Changlings</b> Arcadia or even just <b>Vampires</b> &quot;bloody material&quot; it looks dull. So game about werewolves that is really about Shadow is in long term a bit annoying to me. <b>Forsaken</b> really too much look for me like Spirit Cops. Even <b>Geist</b> is more interesting in this ( even if based on same idea ), because Underworld is so complex and multidimemsional realm to explore, not counting ghost in lands of living. In long run I say Shadow Realm should be more like cWoD Umbra to be more interesting - but this is me.<br /> <br /> But then came <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> spoilers and more and more it looked as more balanced - it looked as game on Harmony on human side battling spiritual beast inside, and trying to equilibrium. When I read that Iron Masters are hunting HUMANS and packs are now werewolf-human-spirit cults - now I'm almost sold. Or at least really interested. I even consider to run Wolf-Blooded game, where before I wouldn't think about it.<br /> <br /> So question for you - what could sell me to <b>Forsaken</b>, once and for all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-15-2014, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:03:22-07:00","id":112833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112829#post112829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So question for you - what could sell me to <b>Forsaken</b>, once and for all?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more of a question for yourself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:22:13-07:00","id":112849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112773#post112773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally find <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thiess_of_Kaltenbrun&amp;quot;]Thiess</a> of Kaltenbrun[/URL] a plenty compelling long-term gaming prospect, particularly when linked to the imagery of hellhounds, the Wild Hunt, berserkers, primal shamanism, a world that runs on a predatory version of the contagion principle, and the complicated reputation of dogs and wolves as a whole, but to each their own.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a pretty cool story. Just not the one I really want to play out in an RPG. But yeah, to each their own. I don't begrudge Forsaken for being what it is. It's actually a very cool game, even though it's not quite to my taste in the default fluff. But I do enjoy it, just in a different wayz","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:23:38-07:00","id":112852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112755#post112755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it you haven't read about Bale Hounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. I get that the &quot;sell your soul to the devil for a good cause/the right reason&quot; theme at can occur with them. In general though, they come across as more Cthulhu cultist then Dorian Grey. Also I kinda disliked the Maeljin stuff. Mainly because it never felt like it &quot;fit&quot; to me. Even the later fluff from other game lines that paints them as Dukes of the Inferno and Rulers of sub-realms within the Lower Depths still did not really make me like them. I feel they are little bit &quot;bolted on&quot; to be the &quot;ultimate evil&quot; in a gameline that already has a load of pretty damn evil things. <br /> <br /> Honestly I'm kinda hoping that the Idigam kinda replace them in the new Chronicle book and the &quot;big bad&quot;, as for all my issues with the Idigam I feel they have a much more solid thematic link back to the Forsaken and the setting as a whole. Alternatively I'd kinda like the Maeljin to get the Brood treatment in Blood and Smoke, namely their not in the core, because various other things make their previous iteration largely redundant (the new take on the Crone and the Strix being around) but they will be covered in a splat book with a brand new take that fits the new setting fluff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112755#post112755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We told him how it clicked, or didn't, for us. If he's too intellectual for for it, that's him. Not everyone is going to like every game, and if you come at it with the intention of not liking it, nothing's going to change.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's no one here who's enjoyed every game they've ever encountered, so lets cut the guy some slack and let him see things how he wants to see them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks again for indulging me and actually replying to a thread that is kinda calling the game the forum is about into question. Once again, people on the WoD boards are much friendlier then a lot of other places I've been. <br /> <br /> I would not say I am coming at Werewolf with the intention of not liking it. Like I said, despite all the so-so things I have to say about it, it's got some sorta hook in me, otherwise I would not keep getting drawn back to it and scratching my head. <br /> <br /> I don't know if I'm too intellectual for the game (god I sound like an ass saying that) but I do have a strong intellectual/analytically buy line into my roleplay. So if anyone has a buy line into Werewolf that feeds that aspect at all, go for the pitch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112755#post112755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These were the first few things that drew me into Forsaken and that last statement is bolded for a reason. It's what is the foundation of Forsaken to me. Territory, Tribes, The People....all these terms make it clear to me what their focus is supposed to be - home and family. Threats from without and threats from within are always looming because the Uratha only have so much they can call their own and so many things are trying to take it away from them. Spirits, Ridden, Pure, your own Rage.....all of them could easily bring the entire house of cards down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that Werewolf is at its best (in my opinion) when its stripped right back to the personal aspect. When the focus is small and tight on the individual and the surrounding friends/family/living area. Like you said, this makes it a lot like Hunter, but comes at the issues in a different way. <br /> <br /> As I've mentioned previously, I find the idea or a larger culture of Werewolves (the Tribes) to be a big turn off. Some aspect of the Tribes, like the need for specialists in a particular field e.g. spirits or humans makes sense to me. The whole idea of a world-wide culture that has these big spirit overseers (the First Born) that people can actually directly interact with, that is what causes some cognitive dissidence for me. Once again, kinda hoping for some minimization of that aspect in Idigam Chronicles. <br /> <br /> Likewise, as with the Papa Bears quote the whole 10 feet tall but having conversations, wielding giant weapons, practicing weird martial arts and odd magic rituals, all of that just makes me unplug I think. It's a bridge too far for me when it comes to tone within the NWoD. I liked that in the Forsaken core the War Form was something measured in rounds and you used it to KILL THINGS in a wave of fury, tooth and claw, that it, that's Werewolf. The moment later books added giant weapons and people doing magic in war form I switched off. Though weirdly I kinda liked the shape shifting fighting style (Tooth and Claw I think it was called) as the fluff seemed to fit the idea of a being that could shape-shift fighting and using all the tools they had in their arsenal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112755#post112755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are Byronic heroes; they're also heroes in the classical sense. Werewolf takes the more cynical approach to classic heroes, which is that they're kinda jerks, and they fight over pride, and while they accomplish great things, it's just as often &quot;great&quot; as in &quot;great and terrible&quot; than as in &quot;great and good.&quot; Werewolves as classical heroic archetypes includes characters like Achilles and Oddyseus and Beowulf. Hercules killed his wife and kids in a fit of anger, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again I think I have some cognitive dissidence on this point. Hero's of the classics, legends and saga's or not necessarily &quot;good&quot; or &quot;nice&quot;, sure, no problem with that. I can get on-board with that idea. It's just not a troupe or idea I've ever connected to or tried to connect to the stories, legends and myths of Werewolves. The two don't have an obvious link in my head. Which is maybe why I'm not fully appreciating this aspect of Forsaken. <br /> <br /> I think a way or reconciling the idea is looking at Werewolf as Papa Bear mentions through the lens of Shamanism and Animism an the shape-shifting mythology in the history of these traditions. I can draw a link between Shamanic magic users Byronic Heroes, that does click for me. <br /> <br /> So I guess we then get into discussion about semantics. This ends up with us in the same talk that some people talk about with Demon, that its a misnamed game because Demon the Descent is not really about Demons (something I would argue is not actually the case), and I don't want to be that guy, because almost everyone I've ever seen start that argument has been a jerk locked into a very rigid idea (usually Aramaic/Judo-Christian) of what a Demon can be. I don't want to be the equivalent for Werewolf. <br /> <br /> \u200bCan anyone point to a source of media e.g. movie, Tv Show, Book that they felt captured the themes or general tone of what they see a Forsaken game as being?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:39:39-07:00","id":112874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112852#post112852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. I get that the &quot;sell your soul to the devil for a good cause/the right reason&quot; theme at can occur with them. In general though, they come across as more Cthulhu cultist then Dorian Grey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely the wrong sort of association. The Maeljin aren't the Abyss, they're human horror. People who lose themselves to their vices are in no way unnatural or uncommon. The Bale Hound philosophy isn't about alienation from humanity or worship of Outer Evil, it's about human vices, human emotions and human feelings gone wrong. What makes the Bale Hounds tragic, sympathetic figures is that their horror is human horror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112852#post112852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCan anyone point to a source of media e.g. movie, Tv Show, Book that they felt captured the themes or general tone of what they see a Forsaken game as being?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sons of Anarchy; specifically the themes of taking on responsibility, personal growth and the sacrifice that comes with it. There's also the pack, the rage, the idea of territory, the concept of using the tools of the barbarian to help ordinary people (and in doing so, alienating oneself irrevocably from ordinary people), fatherhood and the responsibility thereof, etc. Plus lots and lots of violence. Sons of Anarchy is a fantastic source for Werewolf: the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Also, I maintain that Buffy: the Vampire Slayer is just as great a source. There's the grim duty of hunting bad things, there's the pack, there's ugly, double-edged supernatural powers that only serve to alienate those who use them from humanity; themes of family, responsibility, and of course the whole puberty/coming of age analogy that's at the core of the Forsaken mythology. It's a far darker series than many people think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T12:43:53-07:00","id":112877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112852#post112852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCan anyone point to a source of media e.g. movie, Tv Show, Book that they felt captured the themes or general tone of what they see a Forsaken game as being?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal favorite source for Forsaken is the TV show Criminal Minds.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know, no werewolves. But they are a pack of hunters who specialize in a very unique type of prey that can be anyone and anywhere and be just as dangerous as any predator. They can blend in or be totally obvious, but good at hiding. They can have all different kinds of motivations for why they do what they do and various methods. Only by taking the time to study them and understand them can the prey be caught. And all different methods are used to capture them, and when all else fails, <b>open fire!</b><br /> <br /> Also, the Pack is clearly a family, sometimes closer to the team than their own families. While the territory aspect is gone, they still get asked to protect a certain location and deal with the problem there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 04-14-2014, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T13:39:49-07:00","id":112913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112874#post112874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Precisely the wrong sort of association. The Maeljin aren't the Abyss, they're human horror. People who lose themselves to their vices are in no way unnatural or uncommon. The Bale Hound philosophy isn't about alienation from humanity or worship of Outer Evil, it's about human vices, human emotions and human feelings gone wrong. What makes the Bale Hounds tragic, sympathetic figures is that their horror is human horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point. <br /> <br /> Still, I don't think the material on the Maeljin really supports them as a &quot;human&quot; horror. Yes they are a &quot;hot blooded&quot; cosmic evil, the embodiment of the seven deadly sins and the many other vices of mankind (or they are at least beings that feed of such negative/dark impulses). At the end of the day though, they are still incarnations of base evil on an epic scale with motivations and thought processes mainly beyond mankind. Well, beyond the general edicts of &quot;make more sin/vice happen&quot; and &quot;reap souls to feed our eternal hunger&quot;. <br /> <br /> Wrestling with the dark emotions and drives people have and turning that up to 11 is a good way of framing what the Maeljin stand for in a personal and human way. Very &quot;Temptation of Christ&quot; for sure, and very much the idea of it being the &quot;easy&quot; road in a game about making choices that will effect you for the rest or your life (to use the growing up analogy some more). <br /> <br /> Most of what I've seen written on the Maeljin followers paints them more towards the Chaos Cultist (to use a Warhammer 40K reference, sorry if that does not translate well, I know its got some traction cross-culturally but its still very British) vibe. Falling for understandable reasons to beings that embody extreme version of human emotion and are kinda unknowable. The fact that you get twisted in your aims, goals and methods along the way until your nothing but a bastardization of the person you used to be is all only really noticeable once you've fallen so far that your never coming back. Its a very emotionally charged version of the classic &quot;power corrupts&quot; troupe. <br /> <br /> Still I think it does kinda suffer from the same problem a lot of versions of that troupe do. Namely that if people have been doing this sort of thing for centuries/millennia and every single one of them has ended up evil and twisted or dead and this fact has been recorded as a warning to the &quot;normal&quot; members of a given culture then you have to be sorta brain-dead or kinda evil to start out with to walk that particular path. <br /> <br /> Sorry, the above is an unfair generalization. Its fair to say that the best stories happen when you play the &quot;desperation&quot; card in regards to this troupe, that people only go talk to the evil power source when they have no choice or feel they have no choice. Alternatively the &quot;hubris&quot; idea works well too, someone believing they are so strong willed or righteous that they can use the evil power without being corrupted by it (and being inevitably proven wrong) also works. <br /> <br /> Even then though, that leaves the desperate, hubristic, kinda evil or blind to fall into the Maeljin's clutches. That's a pretty select group and really only half its number are sympathetic in any way. <br /> <br /> Like I said before, I really enjoy bits of Werewolf's fluff but the Maeljin are really the bit that has never sat well with me. I like the concept of Bale Hounds, because I am a big believer in the &quot;dark reflection&quot; troupe. I'm hoping that they get shipped over as Werewolf followers of the Idigam rather then the Maeljin in the new Chronicle book. <br /> <br /> I think Strider1276 is writing the Antagonist section? Maybe he can tell us if the Maeljin are in the new Chronicle Book? Unless that would be a massive spoiler, but considering the thing is called the IDIGAM chronicle, I'm betting its not the biggest reveal people are waiting for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T13:54:45-07:00","id":112919,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds can ascend to a Maeladar after their deaths, becoming a Maeltinet and pretty much immortal. Considering it's the World of Darkness, joining the Bale Hounds is hedging your bets with the winning side. Forsaken doesn't have the Apocalypse, but there's no sign of the world becoming a better place anytime soon.<br /> <br /> From there it depends on which view of the Bale Hounds you decide to go with. While there are some examples in the NPCs, they're very few in number, and most fall into the line of 'they meant for the best, made a deal they probably shouldn't have.' Whereas werewolves, like humans, are individuals first and foremost. It wasn't a saintly act that led characters into their First Change. It was chance and genetics. A person who gets a thrill by telling lies may find that, when the existence of what is essentially a god of lies is revealed to them, that their little pleasures can be put to great purpose, and turned from a temporary thrill to a deeply, spiritually rewarding act.<br /> <br /> As for a more intellectual or analytic part of the game, spirits don't have nametags. You'd probably be right if you guessed that that red, white and blue eagle spirit is somehow related to the United States of America, but that walking mirror lined with thorns that screams a glass-shattering scream might be another matter. And while you might be able to gang up on that mirror, as a spirit it's functionally immortal. You can tear it to pieces, but the moment whatever got it fired up in the first place happens again, it'll go around causing trouble again. Sure, there's a lot of leaps, but solving the mysteries behind some of the more problematic spirits can involve very rigorous investigations. And if it turns out whatever's causing that mirror to pop up isn't something you can fix (unless you want to burn down the mirror-factory turned orphanage), then you have to investigate further for a ban, or find some sort of diplomatic way to solve the problem. And diplomacy with spirits....well I'd say it fits more under the Wits stat than Intelligence. Trying to find out a ban can be a long and arduous journey as well, uncovering ancient secrets and symbols, making deals you might not want to make deals with (why would I ever make a deal with a Maeltinet? What if it's the only way to stop this thing?), or a willingness to make other sacrifices.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, you have the whole power vacuum thing going on, except with wider scale consequences. Maybe the Prince died and there was a furor until a new Prince came up, and they favor one covenant over another. But maybe you manage to find the ban of the shrieking mirror and bind it to one place. Now you have to deal with whatever ripples outward from that. Maybe with the shift in resonances, the Silence is growing more powerful. Perhaps due to all the broken windows now there's swarms of shrieking shard spirits slithering through the streets. Maybe the whole mirror thing happened years ago, and the thing was bound beneath the orphanage before the pack disappeared mysteriously. You don't know about that, just that the pack was just like yours, they saw a problem and they went out and dealt with it. And now its your turn, because there's a violent gang of kids out there with mirrors for eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2014, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T14:57:04-07:00","id":112946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112877#post112877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal favorite source for Forsaken is the TV show Criminal Minds.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know, no werewolves. But they are a pack of hunters who specialize in a very unique type of prey that can be anyone and anywhere and be just as dangerous as any predator. They can blend in or be totally obvious, but good at hiding. They can have all different kinds of motivations for why they do what they do and various methods. Only by taking the time to study them and understand them can the prey be caught. And all different methods are used to capture them, and when all else fails, <b>open fire!</b><br /> <br /> Also, the Pack is clearly a family, sometimes closer to the team than their own families. While the territory aspect is gone, they still get asked to protect a certain location and deal with the problem there.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this I think gets at the heart of it very well. I think that's a fantastic example of what Forsaken is all about, and as you point out, no werewolves. Every time I've asked or seen someone ask this question, the answers include a variety of great examples of books, movies, tv shows, etc. that really encapsulate the essence of Forsaken. Very few, if any, of those examples actually contain werewolves. The pop culture image of what werewolves are like, and the themes that are focused on in Forsaken are just different things. That's ok, there's nothing wrong with a unique take on a folkloric creature (and truthfully, the take in Forsaken is in a lot of ways closer to original werewolf lore than the pop culture image of one is). But it does make it difficult for some people to recognize them as that creature if they're only familiar with the pop culture version. Fortunately, it sounds like the new Wolf Blooded are giving us that iconic movie werewolf that many people expect, and the new Harmony is giving us a way for a recently first changed Uratha to go through a process of learning to control her nature by embracing what she is instead of fighting it. Exactly the tools that I feel Forsaken needs to bridge the gap that a lot of newcomers have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T15:42:59-07:00","id":112978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112919#post112919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bale Hounds can ascend to a Maeladar after their deaths, becoming a Maeltinet and pretty much immortal. Considering it's the World of Darkness, joining the Bale Hounds is hedging your bets with the winning side. Forsaken doesn't have the Apocalypse, but there's no sign of the world becoming a better place anytime soon.<br /> <br /> From there it depends on which view of the Bale Hounds you decide to go with. While there are some examples in the NPCs, they're very few in number, and most fall into the line of 'they meant for the best, made a deal they probably shouldn't have.' Whereas werewolves, like humans, are individuals first and foremost. It wasn't a saintly act that led characters into their First Change. It was chance and genetics. A person who gets a thrill by telling lies may find that, when the existence of what is essentially a god of lies is revealed to them, that their little pleasures can be put to great purpose, and turned from a temporary thrill to a deeply, spiritually rewarding act.<br /> <br /> <b>Trying to find out a ban can be a long and arduous journey as well, uncovering ancient secrets and symbols, making deals you might not want to make deals with (why would I ever make a deal with a Maeltinet? What if it's the only way to stop this thing?), or a willingness to make other sacrifices</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting point nofather.<br /> <br /> I've never seen the Maeljin presented via the &quot;necessary evil&quot; element before. Hummm...requires thought that one does.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of keeping Maeltinet around as a sort of &quot;devil you know&quot; theme. Better to have that cordended off wound that you can keep in check and is very, very rarely useful rather then deal with things even more unknowable and amoral (the Idigam and their servants).<br /> <br /> To be fair to the Bale Hounds, I still find them a more interesting &quot;dark reflection&quot; archetype then the Scelesti from Mage (who are presented almost universally as morons or at least utterly self destructive individuals). I just don't think their quite on the same level as the Centimentani and Brood for legitimacy of their philosophy in regards to the default protagonists of their respective game lines. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T16:24:50-07:00","id":112994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112946#post112946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this I think gets at the heart of it very well. I think that's a fantastic example of what Forsaken is all about, and as you point out, no werewolves. Every time I've asked or seen someone ask this question, the answers include a variety of great examples of books, movies, tv shows, etc. that really encapsulate the essence of Forsaken. Very few, if any, of those examples actually contain werewolves. The pop culture image of what werewolves are like, and the themes that are focused on in Forsaken are just different things. That's ok, there's nothing wrong with a unique take on a folkloric creature (and truthfully, the take in Forsaken is in a lot of ways closer to original werewolf lore than the pop culture image of one is). But it does make it difficult for some people to recognize them as that creature if they're only familiar with the pop culture version. Fortunately, it sounds like the new Wolf Blooded are giving us that iconic movie werewolf that many people expect, and the new Harmony is giving us a way for a recently first changed Uratha to go through a process of learning to control her nature by embracing what she is instead of fighting it. Exactly the tools that I feel Forsaken needs to bridge the gap that a lot of newcomers have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think there are two reasons for the new take on werewolves in WoD.<br /> <br /> 1. The traditional view is very close to Vampire. Vampires and werewolves used to be essentially the same thing in European myths, and it still shows. It does not help that while vampires got developed into their own thing, for a long time werewolves stayed as the Jekyll and Hyde type. Having a game that focuses on man vs wolf as the monster is quite farmiliar to how vampire all ready works. To make the games differ, WtA focused on much more the Native American and non-european myths and spirituality. Forsaken follows this route.<br /> <br /> 2. Traditional Werewolves would not make a good WoD game. I'll be honest, one of the best things about WoD is how deep into weirdness it can go. Alongside to being similar to VtR (or B&amp;S), it would not really be very WoD game to have the main splat essentially be normal and then be ST controlled during the full moon. You do need the society there to go all WoD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:02:32-07:00","id":113017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112994#post112994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I think there are two reasons for the new take on werewolves in WoD.<br /> <br /> 1. The traditional view is very close to Vampire. Vampires and werewolves used to be essentially the same thing in European myths, and it still shows. It does not help that while vampires got developed into their own thing, for a long time werewolves stayed as the Jekyll and Hyde type. Having a game that focuses on man vs wolf as the monster is quite farmiliar to how vampire all ready works. To make the games differ, WtA focused on much more the Native American and non-european myths and spirituality. Forsaken follows this route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard this argument before, but I disagree. Werewolf and vampire are (or should be, in my opinion) both about being somewhere between human and monster, and the personal horror comes from reconciling the two. The difference is that vampire is about the descent into monstrosity - you start out mostly human, and over time the reality of having to live as a monster, hiding from the sun and feeding on others to survive, coupled with the long years of immortality grinds away at your Humanity, making you more and more jaded until one day there's nothing left.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, on the other hand, you're totally human right up until you're not. And then you are again, only now you're lying naked in the middle of nowhere covered in your husband's blood. You're not holding off against a slow descent into monstrosity, you have a full-blown monster slumbering inside of you from the moment you're bitten, and you need to either find a way to keep it asleep for good, or at least find a way to gain some semblance of control when you do lose it. And just like with repressed anger, the more you try to hold it back, the worse it gets when it finally breaks free, the only way to live with it is to accept it, to let it out regularly, in the proper time and place, to put your rage to use against the <i>real</i> monsters that are out there. At least, that's what those nutjobs who call themselves &quot;The People&quot; and claim you were born to be one of them keep telling you. Maybe they're right, but is it worth the risk to try to find out? At least, that's what I've always wanted Werewolf to be. And I really don't think it's all that similar to Vampire beyond a very superficial &quot;you frenzy sometimes&quot; mechanic. However...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112994#post112994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Traditional Werewolves would not make a good WoD game. I'll be honest, one of the best things about WoD is how deep into weirdness it can go. Alongside to being similar to VtR (or B&amp;S), it would not really be very WoD game to have the main splat essentially be normal and then be ST controlled during the full moon. You do need the society there to go all WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely true. The game I want would really not be all that fun for most people, and it doesn't really have enough to it to make a full-blown game line around. Which is why I'm so happy to see that it's one of the many play style options that are being accommodated in Idigam. I have always been able to play that character in Forsaken, but it took me a long time to realize that, because it's totally there, the books just don't really focus on it. Now, it's getting more tools to make it easier to shift the focus onto that aspect of the game, without taking away from the heroic or animistic, or fraternal, or any other aspect that also exists in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:43:16-07:00","id":113035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113017#post113017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf, on the other hand, you're totally human right up until you're not. And then you are again, only now you're lying naked in the middle of nowhere covered in your husband's blood. You're not holding off against a slow descent into monstrosity, you have a full-blown monster slumbering inside of you from the moment you're bitten, and you need to either find a way to keep it asleep for good, or at least find a way to gain some semblance of control when you do lose it. And just like with repressed anger, the more you try to hold it back, the worse it gets when it finally breaks free, the only way to live with it is to accept it, to let it out regularly, in the proper time and place, to put your rage to use against the <i>real</i> monsters that are out there. At least, that's what those nutjobs who call themselves &quot;The People&quot; and claim you were born to be one of them keep telling you. Maybe they're right, but is it worth the risk to try to find out? At least, that's what I've always wanted Werewolf to be. And I really don't think it's all that similar to Vampire beyond a very superficial &quot;you frenzy sometimes&quot; mechanic. However...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question here is, then; what would your ideal werewolf be able to do outside changes? Is the only thing that makes them werewolf the curse and the full moon changes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 04-14-2014, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T17:55:11-07:00","id":113038,"title":"","content":"If thats the case they might as well play wolf blooded<br /> <br /> Or a wild child from the chroniclers guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 04-14-2014, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T18:28:36-07:00","id":113049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113035#post113035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the question here is, then; what would your ideal werewolf be able to do outside changes? Is the only thing that makes them werewolf the curse and the full moon changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>There would probably be some residual animalistic traits. Heightened senses, more in touch with base instincts... Ideally, the more the character embraced her wolf side, the stronger those powers would become when she wasn't in wolf form. If her Harmony was out of whack enough, she might not even have any powers in human form at all. But the more she lets the wolf out, the more it affects her human life, giving her advantages like using the higher of Wits or Dexterity for defense like animals do, bonuses to perception rolls for having heightened senses. Maybe bring the animism element into it a bit, become steadily more in touch with the spirit world as you become more wolf-like. But it's also possible to take that too far, become too wolf-like, too spirit. Start taking penalties on normal human social interaction, picking up Bans, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't restrict transformation to full moon only. I actually really like the idea of Auspice, and would have the change happen on the character's Auspice moon, and also with sufficient negative stimuli. This would also be balanced against Harmony. The more in touch with the wolf she is, the easier it would be to trigger a transformation, but the more control over herself she would have when transformed. On one end of the spectrum, she'd only be forced to transform on Auspice moon rise, but when she did it would be full-on Death Rage, no control, no memory of the events afterwords. On the opposite end she'd always be fully in control, but would have a very difficult time keeping from transforming any time something irritates her, which causes its own problems.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, this looks like pretty much exactly the direction Harmony is going in, and even if the details are not quite my ideal version, at least it will have the kind of feel I want from that internal struggle, and the balancing act a Werewolf needs to perform to keep herself from becoming a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T20:24:43-07:00","id":113099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112913#post112913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Strider1276 is writing the Antagonist section? Maybe he can tell us if the Maeljin are in the new Chronicle Book? Unless that would be a massive spoiler, but considering the thing is called the IDIGAM chronicle, I'm betting its not the biggest reveal people are waiting for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I can necessarily say precisely what I wrote, although I think it's safe enough to say the following:<br /> <br /> 1. I did write some baddies, yes, as well as another section in the book.<br /> 2. I am not the only one writing prey.<br /> <br /> I also can't say what is in the book in terms of specific items. That's what Stew's spoilers are for, and if I steal that thunder and spoil something ahead of time...bad things happen. (And by &quot;bad things,&quot; I mean &quot;Jim probably never gets to work on another <b>Werewolf</b> book at least.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I don't know of any <b>Werewolf</b> books on the post-<b>Idigam Chronicle</b> slate, but man, I would love to work on a Bale Hounds project. I have ideas. I hope we can do a Bale Hounds book, and a Pack book, and several other things I'd be keen to work on. Oh, who am I kidding? I'd be happy to work on any <b>Werewolf</b> book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T20:32:50-07:00","id":113102,"title":"","content":"A Bale Hounds book would be fantastic, they deserve a lot more than a single chapter. Their gifts alone were the best themed gifts in the first year of Forsaken.<br /> But I imagine we'll have to get more sales for books like that to be approved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T20:49:03-07:00","id":113105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113102#post113102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Bale Hounds book would be fantastic, they deserve a lot more than a single chapter. Their gifts alone were the best themed gifts in the first year of Forsaken.<br /> But I imagine we'll have to get more sales for books like that to be approved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but that's outside of my bailiwick. I do, however, dearly love the Bale Hounds - which, come to think it, probably says something about me. I'd love to see them get a book and get a change of focus and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T22:56:17-07:00","id":113144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112833#post112833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more of a question for yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't hink so. If youwould asking the same question about <b>Mage</b> I would give you at least 5 selling points on game. Now I see stories in this topic, but not something so simple as, I don't know, <i>enemies are like you</i> or something like this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T23:02:36-07:00","id":113148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112978#post112978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair to the Bale Hounds, I still find them a more interesting &quot;dark reflection&quot; archetype then the Scelesti from Mage (who are presented almost universally as morons or at least utterly self destructive individuals). I just don't think their quite on the same level as the Centimentani and Brood for legitimacy of their philosophy in regards to the default protagonists of their respective game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit off-topic, but Scelasti aren't &quot;morons&quot;, they are deluded. They are blinded by they Hubris and mostly wrecked by traumatic expirance in their lives, like death of loved ones or torments by magic. Basiclly they are PCs, only got twisted by World of Darkness itself with added cosmic ego of Awakaned. With most of Scelasti players can easiy reason. Very reasonable in-setting antagonists.<br /> <br /> As to Bale Hounds I get only that they are Inferno Lords worshipping werewolves. Any true ideas on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T23:20:00-07:00","id":113153,"title":"","content":"You should try reading their section in Blasphemies (still my favorite supplement for Forsaken) if you can get hold of a copy. They aren't necessarily worshippers so much as power hungry werewolves taking the path of least resistance. Not every one of them fits that mold, some really are cult like fanatics, but their allegiances tend to be to themselves first. That's what I took away from it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:02:32-07:00","id":113296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113099#post113099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I can necessarily say precisely what I wrote, although I think it's safe enough to say the following:<br /> <br /> 1. I did write some baddies, yes, as well as another section in the book.<br /> 2. I am not the only one writing prey.<br /> <br /> I also can't say what is in the book in terms of specific items. That's what Stew's spoilers are for, and if I steal that thunder and spoil something ahead of time...bad things happen. (And by &quot;bad things,&quot; I mean &quot;Jim probably never gets to work on another <b>Werewolf</b> book at least.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I don't know of any <b>Werewolf</b> books on the post-<b>Idigam Chronicle</b> slate, but man, I would love to work on a Bale Hounds project. I have ideas. I hope we can do a Bale Hounds book, and a Pack book, and several other things I'd be keen to work on. Oh, who am I kidding? I'd be happy to work on any <b>Werewolf</b> book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair Strider mate. Who else is writing antagonists for the new book? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113099#post113099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit off-topic, but Scelasti aren't &quot;morons&quot;, they are deluded. They are blinded by they Hubris and mostly wrecked by traumatic expirance in their lives, like death of loved ones or torments by magic. Basiclly they are PCs, only got twisted by World of Darkness itself with added cosmic ego of Awakaned. With most of Scelasti players can easiy reason. Very reasonable in-setting antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each to their own mate. I've never seen them presented as such in any Mage game I've ever played in (which is with three different ST's across 5 different games). I've seen them presented as damaged individuals, sure. Most of the time I've seen them presented as utterly mad/insane/morally bankrupt <b>AND LOVING IT</b>! I think they can be taken as the &quot;hubristic fallen mage&quot; archetype (and I think that's their intent in the fluff) but their write ups to make them come across as Cthulhu Cultists a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> Anyway that's massively off-topic and we can leave that there I think. <br /> <br /> Though thinking about this stuff does make the Bale Hounds feel a bit more &quot;personal&quot; in their evil. In so far as their's is a more &quot;selfish&quot; evil, its for their betterment, their advancement, their glory. Rather then serving some higher power in a worshipful manner. Interesting point of contrast I had overlooked. <br /> <br /> Actually, it occurs to me that I am wondering what the new book is going to do with the whole Renown mechanic. I never really liked it as written. I thought it had potential, but needed to be refined and hammered out a bit more then it was. At current it was a little too easy to &quot;blag&quot; Renown if you were a persuasive player and the ST was not being firm on the issue. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:28:18-07:00","id":113313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113296#post113296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each to their own mate. I've never seen them presented as such in any Mage game I've ever played in (which is with three different ST's across 5 different games). I've seen them presented as damaged individuals, sure. Most of the time I've seen them presented as utterly mad/insane/morally bankrupt <b>AND LOVING IT</b>! I think they can be taken as the &quot;hubristic fallen mage&quot; archetype (and I think that's their intent in the fluff) but their write ups to make them come across as Cthulhu Cultists a lot of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You stumble upon something, becuse that was enought for me when I read about Angraboda who was taking Lovecraft novels as literal truth and worship Yog-sototh... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T07:49:37-07:00","id":113321,"title":"","content":"I'm sure we'll get a spoiler one Friday or another.<br /> <br /> I'm in agreement that it was weird, as well, especially given how important it was in regards to getting Gifts, which we've already established had wonky mechanics themselves.<br /> Also the return in investment in 'honorary spirit rank' was pretty underwhelming.<br /> <br /> I could see some persistent renown conditions being available, but we'll see. One of the best things about GMC/Blood and Smoke, is that it definitely encourages more player/storyteller interaction, rather than encouraging the more common, almost antagonistic relationship it's easy to fall into. So hopefully we'll get more of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T08:23:45-07:00","id":113344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113321#post113321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure we'll get a spoiler one Friday or another.<br /> <br /> I'm in agreement that it was weird, as well, especially given how important it was in regards to getting Gifts, which we've already established had wonky mechanics themselves.<br /> Also the return in investment in 'honorary spirit rank' was pretty underwhelming.<br /> <br /> I could see some persistent renown conditions being available, but we'll see. One of the best things about GMC/Blood and Smoke, is that it definitely encourages more player/storyteller interaction, rather than encouraging the more common, almost antagonistic relationship it's easy to fall into. So hopefully we'll get more of that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that Renown and Gifts should not really be interrelated in the new system. Precisely for the reason you mentioned nofather: Conditions. That's a new aspect of the NWoD system post GMC and I think tying Renown to its own set of Conditions that give you a variety of useful effects is a much better use of the idea of Renown. <br /> <br /> As I mentioned previously on this thread, I have issues with Gifts. In that they seemed really unfocused and in a lot of case un-Werewolf to me. Some made sense and I liked, ones that enhance your wolf nature or help with shapeshifting, or manipulate the Shadow or weather. That all felt kinda &quot;Werewolf&quot; to me. Others...not so much. A lot seemed to be powers that were present &quot;just because&quot; in a lot of ways and that ticked me off. Not to mention they were divided by 101 categories: General, Auspice, Tribe, Renown etc, it all needed to be streamlined. <br /> <br /> Needless to say I'm looking forward to the Friday blog this week, I've got high hopes that at least some of the issues I have are straightened out. <br /> <br /> I guess one thing that bugged me about Gifts was the same thing that bugged me about Requiem 1.0 Disciplines: You needed these powers to do the sorta thing that these Supernatural beings just sorta...do in the legends and stories. <br /> <br /> For me one of the biggest improvements Blood and Smoke introduced was that it made the base Vampire template include a lot more stuff off the bat: Heightened Senses, Night Vision, Predators Aura and the Frenzy alterations. You get all that without putting a single dot of Disciplines on a Blood and Smoke Kindred, so &quot;out of the box&quot; they already feel like the the Vampires presented in a lot of modern media and stories. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping Werewolf gets a similar &quot;bulking&quot; to its template. Shape shifting and regeneration at base are nice, but something like Heightened Sense, a Predators Aura sorta affect and some other things I can't think of off the top of my head would be awesome. That way, even on a &quot;gift lite&quot; Werewolf, you still feel like you get plenty of Supernatural bang for your buck. <br /> <br /> I just finished re-reading the Friday blogs that have already been posted. I completely missed the one on Tribes. I like the idea posited then Tribes are now &quot;what you hunt&quot; while Auspice is &quot;how you hunt&quot;. Likewise, I am very in favour of the idea of Tribe as a loose confederation of Werewolf packs that have &quot;bought into&quot; the concept of the Sacred Hunt for a particular prey. With the idea that the Firstborn act as &quot;living testament&quot; that allows the Tribe specific lore of the Sacred Hunt to survive and propagate among the Werewolf population. <br /> <br /> That's the sorta more decentralized idea that I can see working with Werewolf. I've always felt trying to apply a solid government to them in the same way Vampires have Covenants was a foolish idea. This way Tribe can be global but remain culturally influenced and also be more of an &quot;oath of duty&quot; rather then a political statement (making them more coherent then say Prometheans or Demons but less so then Vampires and Mages, I guess similar level to Changelings and Mummys). <br /> <br /> So yeah, Idigam's got a good vibe for me when it comes to Harmony, Tribe, Wolf Blooded and Pack so far. Really the more the game stresses the idea of Packs being the main social unit while being inclusive of Humans in the form of a cult or gang or organisation with Tribe being very much a background thing, I think I can buy the idea of a &quot;society&quot; of Werewolves. I'm not completely sold, I still want to see what's done with Gifts, Renown and the Idigam themselves (well the antagonists in general really) but its doing for me then any version of Werewolf that's come before it.<br /> <br /> Out of interest what are you guys thoughts on Tribe? Both the original Forsaken flavour and the new Idigam take on them? <br /> <br /> \u200bAlso what would you guys like to see as part of the &quot;inbuilt&quot; Werewolf Template in Idigam?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T08:55:54-07:00","id":113357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113296#post113296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair Strider mate. Who else is writing antagonists for the new book?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I can share on that one, I'm afraid, so I'm going to err on the side of caution. There are a bunch of great people working on this book, though. I hope it's well received. I know I love what I've seen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:54:49-07:00","id":113388,"title":"","content":"Getting out my basket to pick a few nits....<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112994#post112994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtA focused on much more the Native American and non-european myths and spirituality. Forsaken follows this route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, a lot of that <b>IS </b>from European mythologies and spiritual-isms, but they're pre-Christian, so very, very old and most people don't even know they existed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=112946#post112946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this I think gets at the heart of it very well. I think that's a fantastic example of what Forsaken is all about, and as you point out, no werewolves. Every time I've asked or seen someone ask this question, the answers include a variety of great examples of books, movies, tv shows, etc. that really encapsulate the essence of Forsaken. Very few, if any, of those examples actually contain werewolves. The pop culture image of what werewolves are like, and the themes that are focused on in Forsaken are just different things. That's ok, there's nothing wrong with a unique take on a folkloric creature (and truthfully, the take in Forsaken is in a lot of ways closer to original werewolf lore than the pop culture image of one is). But it does make it difficult for some people to recognize them as that creature if they're only familiar with the pop culture version. Fortunately, it sounds like the new Wolf Blooded are giving us that iconic movie werewolf that many people expect, and the new Harmony is giving us a way for a recently first changed Uratha to go through a process of learning to control her nature by embracing what she is instead of fighting it. Exactly the tools that I feel Forsaken needs to bridge the gap that a lot of newcomers have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever someone brings out the &quot;not like the pop culture version&quot;, I just like to point out what the public perception of mages and changelings and wraiths and demons and mummies and Sin-Eaters (WTF are those?) would be.<br /> <br /> The games can never possibly accommodate everybody's perception of what a monster should be, so they have to nail it down and start somewhere.<br /> <br /> And, if you ask me, I'd rather they didn't go too far away from some of the much older legends about the creatures in question. After all, if they kept to just the modern ideas, the vampires would sparkle and the werewolves would have to be shirtless 90% of time time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T10:05:56-07:00","id":113393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113388#post113388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whenever someone brings out the &quot;not like the pop culture version&quot;, I just like to point out what the public perception of mages and changelings and wraiths and demons and mummies and Sin-Eaters (WTF are those?) would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Harry Potter</b> and <b>Dresden Files</b> still be very acurate for <b>Mage</b> themes and even magic system. Comic book <b>Fables</b> and a like media are very <b>Changling</b> like, and only realy problem you could have with vampires - if you would make mistake of omiting <b>True Blood</b>, <b>Blood Ties</b> and any post-Rice modern book ot TV Show without sparkling vampires. With <b>Forsaken</b> you don't have anything that connects werewolves with themes that games want to evoke. Real equivalent of <b>Forsaken</b> is only <b>Geist</b>, and this system has much supperior their realm as center idea. It's really is basiclly compering <b>Book of Shadow</b> to <b>Bood of Dead</b>, and they narrative potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T10:08:59-07:00","id":113397,"title":"","content":"Tribes are less global institutions and more bickering families. Then when it really comes down to it, generally you are going to support your pack over someone who ranks up there with an uncle three times removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T10:14:04-07:00","id":113403,"title":"","content":"I'd actually recommend reading the skinner series. Of course it shows mostly what hunters would be like but the full blood are a relatively good exemple of how terrifying it would be to face a shapeshifting beast that heals from everything like the forsaken do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:35:40-07:00","id":113446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113388#post113388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting out my basket to pick a few nits.... Actually, a lot of that <b>IS </b>from European mythologies and spiritual-isms, but they're pre-Christian, so very, very old and most people don't even know they existed. Whenever someone brings out the &amp;quot;not like the pop culture version&amp;quot;, I just like to point out what the public perception of mages and changelings and wraiths and demons and mummies and Sin-Eaters (WTF are those?) would be. The games can never possibly accommodate everybody's perception of what a monster should be, so they have to nail it down and start somewhere. And, if you ask me, I'd rather they didn't go too far away from some of the much older legends about the creatures in question. After all, if they kept to just the modern ideas, the vampires would sparkle and the werewolves would have to be shirtless 90% of time time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mages: Dresden Files, the Sorcerer'sApprentice, arguably Harry Potter. Changelings: not terribly common in pop culture, but Fables is a good example. Arguably Grimm, arguably Once Upon a Time. Wraiths: not an nWoD game line. Mummy: haven't played it, but I can't imagine they're all that different from The Mummy. Demon: aesthetically they are very different from most pop culture Demons, and unsurprisingly, a lot of people take issue with that. I don't, but I still consider it a weak point of the core Demon book that it played up the machine aspect too much and didn't make it clear enough that they can as easily be totally non-mechanical. Sin-Eaters: Human/Gost hybrids, while also not very common in pop culture, tend to very closely resemble Geist. Danny Phantom, though a kid's show, is a great example of a more lighthearted take on Geist, and the upcoming Shadows of Mordor is almost literally Geist in Middle Earth. Like I said, there's nothing wrong with a line doing its own take on the creature type. I love a lot of things in Forsaken that are rare or nonexistent in pop culture werewolves. But the focus of the books is too far removed from many people's expectations for some people to enjoy. Once again, I don't expect the game to change its entire identity. But I am glad that some more iconic werewolf stuff is making its way into the game, such as the new Wolf Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:48:06-07:00","id":113456,"title":"","content":"The only real similarities between Harry Dresden and the other Mage examples to Mage are they do magic. With Fables is that they live among humankind.<br /> <br /> Werewolf does werewolf things. You turn into a bestial human, a monstrous wolfman, a hulking wolf, or a regular wolf, all pretty much staples of iconic werewolf media. You have the chance to do it while emotionally amped up, as well, falling into Kuruth and slaughtering whatever you might find. Also, after the First Change, if you try and resist what you are, you're going to regret it.<br /> <br /> What more is there to the majority of werewolf fiction?<br /> <br /> Spread it to others.<br /> Sex a lot (could still happen, it's just not emphasized in the books).<br /> Can cure yourself by killing the dude who gave it to you.<br /> And blackout shapeshifting, where you don't know what happened.<br /> <br /> The problem with the comparisons to other media is that people pick and choose what they want. And it's not a matter of the game not reflecting fiction in general, as much as not accurately matching one specific piece of fiction that they prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2014, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:54:27-07:00","id":113459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113313#post113313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You stumble upon something, becuse that was enought for me when I read about Angraboda who was taking Lovecraft novels as literal truth and worship Yog-sototh... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD: Inferno, page 33</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cYog-Sothoth is the key, don\u2019t you know?\u201d Angrboda chuckled and writhed in his shackles like a smooth white worm newly exposed to the daylight. Movran checked his chains and corrected a little rune, then bent down to the Scelestus\u2019 grimacing face.<br /> \u201cI\u2019ve got that one in paperback. I read it when I want to cheer myself up with escapist fiction. I\u2019m here about something real: this.\u201d Movran shoved the wrinkled contract in Angrboda\u2019s face. That elicited a big, honest laugh. On his thin frame, it looked like a seizure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, &quot;Yog-Sothoth is the key&quot; is a direct Lovecraft quote, as Movran's reaction indicates. He's cracking a joke. He is taunting his captors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T13:12:39-07:00","id":113505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113456#post113456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only real similarities between Harry Dresden and the other Mage examples to Mage are they do magic. With Fables is that they live among humankind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a <b>Dresden</b> reader ( yet ), but my players are and I watched TV series. From what I see, beside little details with magic, <b>Dresden Files</b> is very <b>Mage: Awakening</b> like. You have hubristic wizards in secret society, Consillium/White Consil, even Dresden himself have Ghost Familliar. I would say it's close enought for start, with all the tales based on how power corrupts mages. And then going in to crossover parts of WoD universe. Literela series about mages, with correct themes of game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With <b>Forsaken</b> we have what? <b>Sons of Anarchy</b> as closest to game setting wise? Not very werewolf to me. But I will try to watch it now, and interprete SoA as <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> pack example with Reaper as Totem. Maybe this will make a click for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T13:24:13-07:00","id":113510,"title":"","content":"Teen Wolf.<br /> It's a mixed game, but I know of people who have run their Forsaken chronicles with a similar setup. It fits the theme perfectly, hunt or be hunted, as well as the mood of savage violence and dark tension.<br /> <br /> Even Hemlock Grove's werewolf depicted a more spiritual bent to them (and to everything else).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:02:22-07:00","id":113542,"title":"","content":"I still think the best example I've seen of a group that felt like a &quot;pack&quot; in a show that really played the &quot;us and them&quot; theme up to 11 is <b>The Walking Dead</b>. <br /> <br /> Honestly, to core group of survivors that the show follows (despite its membership changing a fair bit due to the &quot;anyone can die&quot; trope being in effect) really strike me as a group of very different people pulled together out of a need to survive and face the dangers of the world they live in and the duty they have to the ones they love. Some of these people are not at all alike or even have the same values when the series starts, but they bond due to necessity and the extreme situation they find themselves in.<br /> <br /> The guy that you might have found to be a someone who needs anger management classes and a wider education on the idea of racial and sexual equality is the same guy that save your ass a few dozen times in the last week. He might have found you to be an over-educated nabby-pamby academic with no real world experiences, but you've pulled his ass out of the fire and backed him up when it counts. Pretty soon everyone comes to except everyone and a new &quot;family&quot; is formed. <br /> <br /> From what people have been saying, that seems pretty in theme/tone with Forsaken to me. <br /> <br /> Plus zombies vs werewolves thats pretty awesome. Hum...zombie antagonists in Forsaken. Mushroom hosts? Any others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:13:17-07:00","id":113550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113542#post113542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus zombies vs werewolves thats pretty awesome. Hum...zombie antagonists in Forsaken. Mushroom hosts? Any others?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the Devouring Cloud referenced in Tribes of the Moon's Lodge of the Einherjar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:17:06-07:00","id":113553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113542#post113542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus zombies vs werewolves thats pretty awesome. Hum...zombie antagonists in Forsaken. Mushroom hosts? Any others?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rereading <b>Antagonists</b> for my Mage game, and I think interesting could be spirits based zombies lead by revenant intruder... Once more, most intersting angatongists for werewolf aren't in it's base gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:23:36-07:00","id":113556,"title":"","content":"Aside from the aforementioned mushroom hosts, any spirit that's claiming a body, or even the ghost-hosts, mentioned in Predators and presumably turned into Sin-Eaters without the Dark part. Or the eaters of Zmai, also from Predators.<br /> <br /> In one of my own games, someone decided to dispose of a body in the spirit, which led to an undead monstrosity more like a ghoul than a zombie, though he did create more undead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113553#post113553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading <b>Antagonists</b> for my Mage game, and I think interesting could be spirits based zombies lead by revenant intruder... Once more, most intersting angatongists for werewolf aren't in it's base gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Once more? Considering the depth and variety of werewolf's antagonists, I doubt it's ever been said before by anyone who knows what they're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-15-2014, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T15:02:19-07:00","id":113577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113553#post113553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rereading <b>Antagonists</b> for my Mage game, and I think interesting could be spirits based zombies lead by revenant intruder... Once more, most intersting angatongists for werewolf aren't in it's base gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiosity, what do you not find interesting about the antagonists in Forsaken?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T15:35:59-07:00","id":113595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113510#post113510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teen Wolf.<br /> It's a mixed game, but I know of people who have run their Forsaken chronicles with a similar setup. It fits the theme perfectly, hunt or be hunted, as well as the mood of savage violence and dark tension.<br /> <br /> Even Hemlock Grove's werewolf depicted a more spiritual bent to them (and to everything else).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, you can totally run Forsaken games that do resonate with pop culture werewolves. That's how I've been able to make the game click for me, because all that standard werewolf stuff is in there. The books (especially the core book) just don't do a great job of making that obvious. It's not really the default focus of the game, unless you chose to make it that. And that's fine, as long as the tools are there to allow people who want a Teen Wolf game to play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:42:59-07:00","id":113734,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin just wants to play Cursed, really.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:57:21-07:00","id":113744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113577#post113577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, what do you not find interesting about the antagonists in Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be presumptive on my part (well maybe a little) but wyrdhamster has already mentioned previously in the thread that he is not a huge fan of the Shadow and its inherent animistic nature. I suspect his issue with Forsaken is that the majority of its antagonists find their home/origin/nature defined to some extent by the Shadow. <br /> <br /> I can voice my thoughts on the antagonists within the Forsaken gameline with a little more confidence however, I'm kinda fascinated to here a writers thoughts on these same issues so yeah.<br /> <br /> Form what I remember (considering I have not read a Forsaken book since about 2010) their Antagonists roughly are:<br /> <br /> <b>Other Werewolves:</b> Divided into: The Pure, Bale Hounds and rival Forsaken Packs your PC's have issues/history with. <br /> <br /> <b>Spirits:</b> Divided into: Mageth, inherently &quot;negative&quot; spirits of concepts such as murder, rape etc. Arguably any spirit that screws with stuff on the wrong side of the Gauntlet. <br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Hosts:</b> Divided into: Urged or Claimed<br /> <br /> <b>Shards:</b> Spider, Rat, Raven, Locust, Mushroom, Snake, Wolf? (Not sure about that last one, also sure I am missing some) <br /> <br /> <b>Maeljin:</b> Divided into: Maelinet and Maelin I believe. If your using Inferno then the &quot;possessed&quot; from that book might come under this group as well. <br /> <br /> <b>Idigam:</b> Can't speak to any changes in the new book, but to my understanding at current they are primordial spirits with no reflective aspect in the material world, making them &quot;impossible&quot; my normal spirits standards. May or may not embody the every idea of &quot;change&quot; or &quot;evolution&quot; in some regards, subject to debate. All are monstrously powerful and basically impossible to permanently kill, above and beyond even normal spirits. <br /> <br /> Out of those 6 categories all but Other Werewolves (and even they involve Spirits (Pack Totems) and the Shadow (using it in warfare) by their nature) are basically spirits in one fashion or another. Just to tie this back to issues wyrdhamster might have for a second.<br /> <br /> I like the rival pack thing because its very Human and no one is out-and-out the bad guy. Its basically like watching to human gangs go to war in something like The Wire. <br /> <br /> The Pure never did anything for me, fanatical extremist Werewolves that believe in a return to a more primitive world where they are the top-dogs is a little 1-note for me. They remind me just a little bit to much of some of the 2nd Ed Masquerade stuff on the Sabbat, before they got fleshed out to be a more complex socio-religious apocalypse cult/church of Caine. I can't even put my finger on what I feel is lacking about them, only that they feel slightly redundant to me. <br /> <br /> Bale Hounds, well I've already talked on this issue a bit in this thread. Thought later posters comments have got me thinking about them in more Faust/Dorian Grey aesthetics that I can dig. So I guess I could say I like them as complex self-involved villains and not cackling infernalists. <br /> <br /> Spirits, kinda already made my supposition here. Either you enjoy Spirit plot or you don't. I don't have a huge issue with it, I know people that do. Only so many times you can play the twenty questions game of &quot;what sort of spirit is it&quot; and &quot;what are its bans and how do we find them&quot; etc. I find making my Shadow more like the other world of the Silent Hill games and its denizens about a similar sorta tone is enough that the creepy aesthetics and atmosphere is enough to keep players engaged for the most part (at least in the context of Hunter and Mage, never run Werewolf). <br /> <br /> Spirit Hosts add a human element that can be interesting and throw up moral dilemmas for sure. Particularly because possession can make a plot deeply personal I feel. Ran a possession plot as part of a Hunter Campaign and it was the plot that I got the most positive feedback from my players on. I think it grounds or internalized Spirit plot which can otherwise be very, very external in nature. <br /> <br /> Shards are creepy and other and have a slightly different feel from your default Spirit Antagonists, but they are a &quot;known&quot; threat a lot of the time. The People know how to deal with them, what they do and where they come from. I've seen game where clearing out the Rat and Spider nests is almost treated like janitor duty by the PC's because its just seen as &quot;a job&quot; inhered from Father Wolf and with little real feeling of feel (though a healthy respect for the danger involved). <br /> <br /> Maeljin I've already shared my thoughts about. I think they are a bit of an ill fit and feel slightly bolted on to the setting (bit like the Pure actually). I liked the that later books in the NWoD game line kinda explained them more (Inferno) and I'm even happy to include some of the Mage fluff on them (Summoners/Imperial Mysteries). So I guess coming at them from mainly either a core NWoD viewpoint or a Hunter/Mage viewpoint they look a bit odd/off in Werewolf, despite it being the game that introduced them. Let me put it this way, in my games I consider it cannon that the Maeljin and their ephemeral servants are NOT actually Spirits but demons/denizens of a realm within the lower depths. <br /> <br /> I think I'd like them to be refluffed to be more &quot;equal opportunity&quot; bad guys. So instead of just showing up in the Wounds in the Shadow they have a presence in the Astral, Hedge and Underworld that way the game lines that interact with those realms each get a piece of the puzzle in regards to the Maeljin/Archdukes of the Inferno/Denizens of the Lower Depths from their particular supernatural races viewpoint. Still, have said supernaturals be at least a little genre savvy e.g. Werewolves realize that Maeljin stuff is not actually Spirit related, more a case of something &quot;other&quot; intruding into the Shadow. <br /> <br /> Idigam I actually like as an idea. Werewolf I think needed a grounded &quot;big bad&quot; that could be held up as such. Requiem likewise needed something similar and the Strix provide that roll really well. I have issue with some of the fluff around them (mutant babies? thrown to the moon? moon landings?) as its a bit weird. The core idea of Spirits that &quot;should not be&quot; and &quot;don't play by the rules&quot; and represent ideas so abstract and primordial then sentient life can't really grasp onto them without going kinda nuts. It gives something that is definitively &quot;other&quot; in a game that is already kinda full of a sense of the &quot;other&quot;. <br /> <br /> Needless to say, I'm dying to see what the writers come up with for them in the new book, if they get the same sort of extra development and thematic shot in the arm that the Strix did in Blood and Smoke I'd be tempted to use them as major villains in any game line in the NWoD (save maybe Vampire and Mummy). <br /> <br /> \u200bThis reply got out of hand, was supposed to be shorter then this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T19:31:48-07:00","id":113756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113734#post113734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin just wants to play Cursed, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, that was a weird movie, but it did have some of the things I like in werewolves. Not really enough to it to make a game out of though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T19:32:31-07:00","id":113757,"title":"","content":"There's also the Ancient Horrors, from the last chapter of Predators. Remnants of a bygone age, they are neither spirit nor Host, yet don't have a natural origin (no evolution here). Among others are the Nuigim, who cannot be seen (not merely invisible, things done to see it will fail, paint and other markers of its physical presence just fading away), and the Zmai, sort of like one of Dune's sandworms (a big, long worm) but covered in this oozing ichor that is not only unnaturally tempting to eat, but wildly addictive and transformative, turning its followers into pale, tumor-ridden zombies.<br /> <br /> And although they only had one entry (though the mechanics for making them exists with the Idigam), there are the su'ur. This is a spirit threat. The Idigam Gurdilag (and presumably others) can take out peoples souls, or spirits, and shove them wherever they want. When done with humans this usually just makes something similar to duguthim, the claimed. But, the Gurdilag liked to experiment and, finding that werewolves were part spirit, decided to change them, creating the su'ur, or Empty Wolves. The sample pack from the Rockies consists of an alpha combined with a powerful Azlu, a giant combined with a spirit of cannibalism, and a shaman combined with a spirit of regret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:07:29-07:00","id":113764,"title":"","content":"Hawthorn, I believe a big portion of why Forsaken appeals to me is not because of the antagonists, or the shadow, or whatever setting the books portray, but the relationship that being in a pack represents. If you have any siblings, have you ever had a quarrel with them which may have involved beating them up (lovingly of course)? With Vampires, you have clans and coteries and all of that, but the grand scheme is more of a political war than anything else.<br /> <br /> With Werewolf, your pack is your life, your daily bread, and even closer than family. You fight amongst each other, you may even lead them, but at the end of the day, even the omega of the pack has something to contribute. During this entire time, you don't wonder what their hidden agenda is, nor do you feel like you are being manipulated as some pawn in a giant chess game, but you know deep down inside that the wolf must hunt, and so you do.<br /> <br /> I learned early on that if you don't like a setting, ignore it or downplay it. If you are not a fan of the shadow or spirit antagonists, relegate it to the background. You can spend dozens of sessions rooting out a Vampire cabal or a Coven of Witches, maybe even a mage or two who decides to setup shop on your turf without permission. Why? Because you claimed this area and your not going to let some stinky undead thing or some weird human who can't even perform magic in front of humans to tell you what to do.<br /> <br /> In one of my games, a Promethean decided that he was tired of traveling and settled down in the territory for a bit too long. My players blew him up by packing a Jeep full of explosives and ramming it into him at 70 MPH while the radio blasted Crazy by Aerosmith. The shadow didn't even come into play, but holy hell did it make a big bang!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:24:08-07:00","id":113774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113764#post113764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hawthorn, I believe a big portion of why Forsaken appeals to me is not because of the antagonists, or the shadow, or whatever setting the books portray, but the relationship that being in a pack represents. If you have any siblings, have you ever had a quarrel with them which may have involved beating them up (lovingly of course)? With Vampires, you have clans and coteries and all of that, but the grand scheme is more of a political war than anything else.<br /> <br /> With Werewolf, your pack is your life, your daily bread, and even closer than family. You fight amongst each other, you may even lead them, but at the end of the day, even the omega of the pack has something to contribute. During this entire time, you don't wonder what their hidden agenda is, nor do you feel like you are being manipulated as some pawn in a giant chess game, but you know deep down inside that the wolf must hunt, and so you do.<br /> <br /> I learned early on that if you don't like a setting, ignore it or downplay it. If you are not a fan of the shadow or spirit antagonists, relegate it to the background. You can spend dozens of sessions rooting out a Vampire cabal or a Coven of Witches, maybe even a mage or two who decides to setup shop on your turf without permission. Why? Because you claimed this area and your not going to let some stinky undead thing or some weird human who can't even perform magic in front of humans to tell you what to do.<br /> <br /> In one of my games, a Promethean decided that he was tired of traveling and settled down in the territory for a bit too long. My players blew him up by packing a Jeep full of explosives and ramming it into him at 70 MPH while the radio blasted Crazy by Aerosmith. The shadow didn't even come into play, but holy hell did it make a big bang!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it wrong that my first through when reading this was:<br /> <br /> That poor Promethean...<br /> <br /> Sorry I have all the sympathy in the world for the Created. Really hope Promethean gets a chronicle book.<br /> <br /> Anway, I'm not trying to focus the conversation on Antagonists specifically, just that Strider1276 who we know is a writer on Idigam and is writing some antagonist stuff asked about another posters issues with the existing takes on the main Antagonists of Forsaken. I felt compelled to butt-in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I get the pack thing as a draw. It is something I can understand, nice to have a group identity and not worry about horrid manipulation by the main NPC's (which is pretty much the bread-and-butter of Vampire). I'm an only child, but I've been on the verge of blows with friends a few times. Maybe that's why Forsaken does not click, I'm to solipsistic ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:40:59-07:00","id":113781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113774#post113774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it wrong that my first through when reading this was:<br /> <br /> That poor Promethean...</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone is entitled to their own opinions :P<br /> <br /> I see what you mean with your antagonists comments especially with Stew and Strider giving us juicy tantalizing tidbits. From my point of view, the problem with Forsaken was never with the antagonists, but the lack of scope compared to the other games. If you have fantastic antagonists, but the game revolves in the simplest form as a hack and slash, then there is not much leeway. Other gamelines such as Vampire and Changeling allow hack and slash, political intrigue, etc in a much more robust manner which helps a ton.<br /> <br /> Still, I have confidence that the lesson was learned and heaven knows there has been years worth of time to collect feedback and popular opinion on the matter at hand. We very well might see a resurgence of Werewolf popularity not seen since that actor took off his shirt in Twilight and promised to have puppies with that girl who had the same level of common sense as a catatonic squirrel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:49:44-07:00","id":113787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113781#post113781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone is entitled to their own opinions :P<br /> <br /> I see what you mean with your antagonists comments especially with Stew and Strider giving us juicy tantalizing tidbits. From my point of view, the problem with Forsaken was never with the antagonists, but the lack of scope compared to the other games. If you have fantastic antagonists, but the game revolves in the simplest form as a hack and slash, then there is not much leeway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had a hard time putting my misgivings (beyond the mechanics) into words but there you go and do it. With all the stuff that can happen with the shadow, incomprehensible beings from the moon, being descended from the spirit of the moon and an ancient prehistoric beast king, up against kin who are trying to turn the world into a crazed hunting ground bereft of civilization, and all the other antagonists, the game comes down to, &quot;cut out your territory, defend it.&quot; Obviously, it being a rpg, you can do whatever you want, fly to Russia and hunt down Rasputin's Occult Wolves, create a new Pentex, become a spirit of great power and influence, eat gods. But from start to finish the books put the majority of focus on what would later be called first tier, occasionally dipping into second when you have to deal with neighboring packs or lodges.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the whole wolf must hunt thing will break them out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-16-2014, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T21:16:32-07:00","id":113808,"title":"","content":"Having a problem with the Shadow in Forsaken is like having a problem with the Hedge in Changeling.<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin: I mean The Cursed, from the first chapter of the Chronicler's guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T21:19:51-07:00","id":113814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113781#post113781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you mean with your antagonists comments especially with Stew and Strider giving us juicy tantalizing tidbits. From my point of view, the problem with Forsaken was never with the antagonists, but the lack of scope compared to the other games. If you have fantastic antagonists, but the game revolves in the simplest form as a hack and slash, then there is not much leeway. Other gamelines such as Vampire and Changeling allow hack and slash, political intrigue, etc in a much more robust manner which helps a ton.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think scope is necessarily an issue with Forsaken. I actually the fact that the game runs at Tier 1 90% of the time. If you want to end up fighting Rank 6+ Spirits in the deep Shadow and throwing it up to Tier 3 you can and that's a great way of ending a story thread or even a whole campaign. One of things I definitely appreciate from what people have been talking about on this thread is how well Forsaken can be used to create the feeling of a &quot;family&quot; and I think that tone really benefits from saying at Tier 1.<br /> <br /> I agree with the &quot;hack and slash&quot; problem though. A lot of Werewolf seems to be geared towards combat. More so then any of the other Major lines in fact.<br /> <br /> Vampires need to keep the Masquerade, Mages suffer Paradox, Prometheans have disquiet effects linked to transmutation use, Demons are one use of power away from hunter angels showing up.<br /> <br /> Basically, with the exception of Mummy and Giest every line has a big negative for using your powers openly in combat. Werewolf, like those games, does not. Lunacy covers your arse for a lot of stuff when it comes to Humans. Half the time your fighting in another realm and can go all out.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that because Werewolves are designed as a physical primary template that the devs of the previous edition might have got a little locked into the idea of having a physical solution to most problems. Anything that does not have an immediate physical solution can be fixed with research and occult for the most part. I know there was some effort to instill the idea of &quot;spirit&quot; politics but it always felt very &quot;optional&quot; or added-on to me as an after thought.<br /> <br /> I think Forsaken's antagonists reflect this issue. The answer to maraudering spirits,bale hounds, hosts and wound entities is pretty much &quot;hit it till its dead&quot;. Possessed and Idigam fall into the &quot;research&quot; or occult category by necessity (the former only if the pack in question has issues killed the host, otherwise it another &quot;smack it&quot; enemy). The Pure can have a social element of &quot;negotiations&quot; to them, but I feel that's an exception, not a rule and most of the time its werewolf vs werewolf grudge matches.<br /> <br /> I know its been years since I read the books, but until nofather mentioned the idea of having a weak wound and its associated spirits being tolerated as a necessary evil because they &quot;know things&quot; that might help the pack's territory as a whole, I never got the impression or hint from any cannon source that such a thing was even considered by the Forsaken. Really, it all &quot;purge this&quot; and &quot;purify that&quot; in a lot of the Forsaken antagonist write ups.<br /> <br /> Though once again design choices need to be kept in mind. With the base and destructive nature of the Hosts for example, how could one come to a non-violent and non-occult solution to the problem? Its not really a possibility because of the inherent nature of the antagonist, which makes them, in my opinion at least, one-note and less interesting.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has an underlying tone of anger/rage/fury and violence is kinda a natural extension of that. Still, having violence be the solution to 75%+ of the games issues, that falls a little flat with me. Hopefully Idigam will give us more options then the holy trinity of: Hit it, Magic it or research it that the previous edition ran off. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 04-16-2014, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T21:51:08-07:00","id":113831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113577#post113577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, what do you not find interesting about the antagonists in Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are all the Spirits, one way or another. On each game session, seeing dead bodies in beginning I can easily shout &quot;Spirit done it!&quot; and be accurate with 95% chance. Maybe was only those few game sessions I got of <b>Forsaken</b> not enought. Or our ST was very limited in his views. But even I got from corebook reading that real problems are just from Spirits and Spirits-based hybrids in <b>Frosaken</b>. There isn't any variety, only &quot;more of the same&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not too mention that humans become only proper target for hunt in <b>Idigam Chronicles</b> Tribes spoiler, where they were marked by Iron Masters as sacred enemy. I run very human-centric and human based games, coloring hights and lows of our race, so only now I could return to old nWoD theme of &quot;humanity is fu#$ed, we are all flawed&quot; and poppulate my World of Darkness streets with classical murderes, psychopaths and decadents. In orginal <b>Forsaken</b> answer is always &quot;Spirits made me do it&quot;. There isn't place in this game for just normal, down to Earth &quot;he is one twisted men&quot;. Werewolves are so preocupied with Shadow Realm they just can't solve things that make WoD setting it is - just normal, human evil.<br /> <br /> Also, like I wrote ealier, I found Shadow Realm to be sooooo dull in comparison to other gamelines and Spirits ecology is just... coarse. All of them want to eat other spirits to be more powerfull. They don't trick one another. Don't plead. Don't interact in other way than &quot;You listen me all, or I will eat all of you&quot;. To simplistic, and too much reused in whole gameline.<br /> <br /> You could use other werwolves - anything really beside Bale Hounds? Pure are once more, dull monsterous version of Seers of Throne - but the same I could make in vampire, mage, changling and any other gameline. True interesting antagonists come from variety. In <b>Geist</b>, you gave very complex and diverse types of monsters and villians to interfere with players,<b> before</b> you go to players splat itself. <b>Mage</b> I don't say, beuase it completly other leage with multiple dimensions, Abyss, humanity itself as one of main antagonists itself, and any other random mystery. Compared to this all <b>Forsaken</b> with all it &quot;spirits do this, spirits do that&quot; seems really... moldy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T22:30:53-07:00","id":113853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113814#post113814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the &quot;hack and slash&quot; problem though. A lot of Werewolf seems to be geared towards combat. More so then any of the other Major lines in fact.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that because Werewolves are designed as a physical primary template that the devs of the previous edition might have got a little locked into the idea of having a physical solution to most problems. Anything that does not have an immediate physical solution can be fixed with research and occult for the most part. I know there was some effort to instill the idea of &quot;spirit&quot; politics but it always felt very &quot;optional&quot; or added-on to me as an after thought.<br /> <br /> I think Forsaken's antagonists reflect this issue. The answer to maraudering spirits,bale hounds, hosts and wound entities is pretty much &quot;hit it till its dead&quot;. Possessed and Idigam fall into the &quot;research&quot; or occult category by necessity (the former only if the pack in question has issues killed the host, otherwise it another &quot;smack it&quot; enemy). The Pure can have a social element of &quot;negotiations&quot; to them, but I feel that's an exception, not a rule and most of the time its werewolf vs werewolf grudge matches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, reading this sort of thing just makes me sad. There's so much that is wrong here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113814#post113814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its been years since I read the books</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you should really reread them, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T22:39:17-07:00","id":113857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113831#post113831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are all the Spirits, one way or another. On each game session, seeing dead bodies in beginning I can easily shout &quot;Spirit done it!&quot; and be accurate with 95% chance. Maybe was only those few game sessions I got of <b>Forsaken</b> not enought. Or our ST was very limited in his views. But even I got from corebook reading that real problems are just from Spirits and Spirits-based hybrids in <b>Frosaken</b>. There isn't any variety, only &quot;more of the same&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> You could use other werwolves - anything really beside Bale Hounds? Pure are once more, dull monsterous version of Seers of Throne - but the same I could make in vampire, mage, changling and any other gameline. True interesting antagonists come from variety. In <b>Geist</b>, you gave very complex and diverse types of monsters and villians to interfere with players,<b> before</b> you go to players splat itself. <b>Mage</b> I don't say, beuase it completly other leage with multiple dimensions, Abyss, humanity itself as one of main antagonists itself, and any other random mystery. Compared to this all <b>Forsaken</b> with all it &quot;spirits do this, spirits do that&quot; seems really... moldy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ... wrong, mostly. Spirits are not intended to be active forces; mostly - they're reactive in that they're reflections of the Flesh.<br /> <br /> You don't get to face some anger spirit, you'll face the embodied wrath of a teenager about to go on a killing spree in his school. The murder spirit trying to rip your guts out is an idealized reflection of that serial killer who slaughtered a two digit number of people in the city decades ago. The lust spirit trying to seduce you - it's the PC's own repressed feelings of sexuality, trying desperately to find a release.<br /> <br /> When you fight spirits, you don't fight random encounter monsters; you fight things that exist in the Flesh, given spiritual form (and teeth and claws). The Shadow isn't a place of fantasy, it's a place where thoughts and feeling are materialized. This is also why so many of the beings you find there are very difficult to defeat by hitting them (and this is also why Hawthorne is wrong about Werewolf being, mostly, a game about hitting things); you can't kill your own fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 04-16-2014, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T22:45:20-07:00","id":113863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113857#post113857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you fight spirits, you don't fight random encounter monsters; you fight things that exist in the Flesh, given spiritual form (and teeth and claws).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, having <i>just finished rereading the corebook last week</i>, I can confirm this with a direct quote that sums it up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>As an element of horror, spirits inherently represent consequences.</b> When a murderer stalks a city block, killing again and again without being caught, the dangerous spirits that gain strength from his spree are a consequence. They directly represent the ramifications of the murderer\u2019s actions, but they also represent the consequences of others\u2019 failure to catch and stop the murderer. A community that has a secret history of hate may have engendered a powerful spirit threat, one that emphasizes the enormity of their brutal actions when the community\u2019s quiet fa\u00e7ade gives no hint. Most spirits represent the weakness and selfishness of human action, but some also reflect the failings of the Uratha themselves. In the animistic world of <i>Werewolf</i>, spirits are a direct reminder that the evil that goes unseen is just as gruesome a threat. Every action has its consequence, and the pack must be consistently vigilant to fight against those consequences. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T22:48:28-07:00","id":113868,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I think when people who don't really know much about Werewolf are talking about spirits and the Shadow, they are generally ignoring the inherent Silent Hill quality of the Shadow. I think that's missing the entire point of the Shadow and of spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T23:20:16-07:00","id":113875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113868#post113868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I think when people who don't really know much about Werewolf are talking about spirits and the Shadow, they are generally ignoring the inherent Silent Hill quality of the Shadow. I think that's missing the entire point of the Shadow and of spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe not. Compared to the huge variety of WtA's Umbra, the Shadow being solely Silent Hill can be a bit limiting. I love Silent Hill, but I'd rather not have it as an example for all spirit activity (given Silent Hill is a purgatory and so would not fit in every spiritual situation equally well). The latter books did a lot to make the Shadow more easily accesible for the Uratha, which I liked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T23:38:16-07:00","id":113880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113875#post113875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or maybe not. Compared to the huge variety of WtA's Umbra, the Shadow being solely Silent Hill can be a bit limiting. I love Silent Hill, but I'd rather not have it as an example for all spirit activity (given Silent Hill is a purgatory and so would not fit in every spiritual situation equally well).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the <i>predatory mythic reflection of the world.</i> Silent Hill is not a <i>perfect</i> comparison, but it gets the job done in terms of &quot;this place filled with the symbolism of your failings and the failings of those preceding and surrounding you will consume you if you do not overcome it in some fashion.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T00:09:38-07:00","id":113887,"title":"","content":"You can't defeat the Pure by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. You'll quite simply die trying. Their packs are larger than yours. They have stronger, more numerous spirit allies; and they have hate, determination and the absolute certainty that they're fighting for the right side.<br /> <br /> The Pure can be beat by playing it smart. Isolating them from their spirit allies. Stealing or destroying their resources (loci, fetishes, wolf-blooded, money). Cornering part of the pack in places where you can reasonably kill them off. Breaking their hate, taking away their determination and certainty.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat Bale Hounds by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. How would you know who to hit? Bale Hounds often hide among the Forsaken, and it takes surveillance, intuition, persistence and all kinds of social skills and smarts to figure out who the rat in your pack is.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat spirits by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. Have you had a look at the spirit rules? These things are crazy powerful; meaning that the wiser course of action will often be figuring out their weaknesses and how to best exploit them.<br /> Moreover, a spirit you tear apart will quite simply reform and come back to haunt you once it has gathered sufficient essence. Remember how spirits are reflections of the Flesh.<br /> <br /> Spirits are fought by changing the Flesh so that they lack appropriate sources of essence. Solve the murder case and bring the murder to justice. Stop the pollution. Conquer your fear. Anything else is just a temporary solution.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat Spirit-Possessed by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. How would you know who to kill? The Possessed cannot easily be perceived, and, as with the Bale Hounds, it takes perception and investigative skills to find them.<br /> <br /> And even if you catch them, they'll just laugh at you and possess the next victim, and you'll be left with a dead human at your feet.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat Spirit-Urged by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. Besides the issue of finding them, Urged are Urged because they in some way attracted a spirit. This is their weakness; this is how you can stop a spirit from Urging a victim. A spirit of hate has no reason or desire to Urge someone who, with the help of his pack, has conquered her hate.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat the Hosts by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. Besides the fact that some are crazy powerful in combat, and all of them cause problems in the Shadow that will only make your job harder, even if you manage tearing one of these critters apart, unless you have prepared yourself well, the Shard will quite simply escape, eat the brain/heart of the next guy and continue to cause trouble. The Hosts attack a pack's territory using methods that don't vary a lot, but they're insanely hard to get rid off permanently. They have been designed so as to be persistent and the next time, they'll know you and your methods, and they'll come prepared.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat Spirit-Claimed by walking up to them and hitting them until they stop moving. Well, actually, you can. Spirit-Claimed explicitely serve the purpose of being mostly low-key opponents that you can actually defeat with nothing but your claws. That doesn't change the fact that they come in wildly varying power levels and with wildly varying abilities, making it almost impossible to predict how they'll cause trouble.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat a person by walking up to him and hitting him until he stops moving. Obviously werewolves can, but in a World of Darkness game, and in a setting where consequences matter, killing humans isn't lightly done.<br /> <br /> Have you noticed how the Idigam also follow this pattern? They're too big and nasty to be killed by walking up to them and hitting them with your claws.<br /> <br /> Also; have you noticed that, of the five auspices, only the Rahu is strongly optimized towards being a fighter?<br /> <br /> It almost seems as if all of the game's antagonists were designed, possibly even intentionally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , to require the player characters to be smart and use various skills above and beyond those of the Rahu in their hunts. Anything else will get a pack killed very soon.<br /> <br /> Werewolves hunt. Battle is not their primary business.<br /> <br /> Personally, I also believe that running hunts is, plot- and story-wise, more interesting that running fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 04-16-2014, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T02:09:54-07:00","id":113929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maeljin I've already shared my thoughts about. I think they are a bit of an ill fit and feel slightly bolted on to the setting (bit like the Pure actually). I liked the that later books in the NWoD game line kinda explained them more (Inferno) and I'm even happy to include some of the Mage fluff on them (Summoners/Imperial Mysteries). So I guess coming at them from mainly either a core NWoD viewpoint or a Hunter/Mage viewpoint they look a bit odd/off in Werewolf, despite it being the game that introduced them. Let me put it this way, in my games I consider it cannon that the Maeljin and their ephemeral servants are NOT actually Spirits but demons/denizens of a realm within the lower depths.<br /> <br /> I think I'd like them to be refluffed to be more &quot;equal opportunity&quot; bad guys. So instead of just showing up in the Wounds in the Shadow they have a presence in the Astral, Hedge and Underworld that way the game lines that interact with those realms each get a piece of the puzzle in regards to the Maeljin/Archdukes of the Inferno/Denizens of the Lower Depths from their particular supernatural races viewpoint. Still, have said supernaturals be at least a little genre savvy e.g. Werewolves realize that Maeljin stuff is not actually Spirit related, more a case of something &quot;other&quot; intruding into the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this I could easily reason, as I was intetersted in running the <b>Inferno</b> game long time and now I see I could run it with werewolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not thought about it before, but if gameline really supports it, it could be interesting short game to run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113863#post113863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, having <i>just finished rereading the corebook last week</i>, I can confirm this with a direct quote that sums it up:</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As an element of horror, spirits inherently represent consequences.</b><i> When a murderer stalks a city block, killing again and again without being caught, the dangerous spirits that gain strength from his spree are a consequence. They directly represent the ramifications of the murderer\u2019s actions, but they also represent the consequences of others\u2019 failure to catch and stop the murderer. A community that has a secret history of hate may have engendered a powerful spirit threat, one that emphasizes the enormity of their brutal actions when the community\u2019s quiet fa\u00e7ade gives no hint. Most spirits represent the weakness and selfishness of human action, but some also reflect the failings of the Uratha themselves. In the animistic world of </i><i>Werewolf</i><i>, spirits are a direct reminder that the evil that goes unseen is just as gruesome a threat. Every action has its consequence, and the pack must be consistently vigilant to fight against those consequences.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You see, this &quot;reflective Silent Hill&quot; always was ommited by my, becuase our previous ST come up with spirits so random, it was a bit pitefull. I could see that cultist ifested Silent Hill-like tow could make interesting <b>Forsaken</b> game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a problem with the Shadow in Forsaken is like having a problem with the Hedge in Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not having problem with Hegde as it is a lat more disjointed realm with Material Plane, and has clear &quot;wicked fairy tale&quot; theme to it. I run interesting sesios in it for both mages and changlings, partialy because I wasn't limited by &quot;scope&quot; - I putted there sunkcen cathedrals, shipwrecks in bogs or just plain old &quot;Pan's Laybirynth&quot;-like maze of shrubs with beast in there. Shadow is much more &quot;it's here and now, only a more scarier&quot; withc is really hard to make on for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T02:54:45-07:00","id":113938,"title":"","content":"Spirits and the Shadow are one of my favourite bits of Forsaken. It's an entire alien world of symbolism and weirdness that's right next to reality, inhabited with its own thronging society of Broods, Descants and Choirs, spirit courts all plotting against one another and clashing over spreading their favoured Resonance. Spirit totems are a brilliant way to get a pack embroiled in Shadow politics; the rise of one particular totem through the Court of electricity and information was a major source of plot and conflict for the pack in the longest W:tF chronicle I've run.<br /> <br /> There's so much you can do with the Shadow, especially when you delve into the <i>history</i> of an area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:16:07-07:00","id":113997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113808#post113808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a problem with the Shadow in Forsaken is like having a problem with the Hedge in Changeling. @Charlaquin: I mean The Cursed, from the first chapter of the Chronicler's guide.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm. Haven't read that book, but I'll have to check it out now. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:53:16-07:00","id":114105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113938#post113938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's so much you can do with the Shadow, especially when you delve into the <i>history</i> of an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the reason as for why I chose Kosovo as the location for my next Werewolf chronicle.<br /> <br /> It won't be a nice game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:39:20-07:00","id":114138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113853#post113853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, reading this sort of thing just makes me sad. There's so much that is wrong here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to ask that you be a little more constructive with you feedback but then you did provide a larger post later in the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113853#post113853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I think when people who don't really know much about Werewolf are talking about spirits and the Shadow, they are generally ignoring the inherent Silent Hill quality of the Shadow. I think that's missing the entire point of the Shadow and of spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair Wyrdhamster runs Mage, which also interacts with the Shadow, though in a different way from Werewolf (or at least to a different end). Yes he's admitted he's not a fan of the realm, but hes going to have a passing familiarity with it form being a Mage ST.<br /> <br /> If you were referring to me well, its been 4 years since I read anything Werewolf, but in that time I've run a long-running Hunter game that used the Shadow and its Spirit denizens a fair bit.<br /> <br /> To be clear on a point in case anyone missed it previously: <b>I like the Shadow and I don't have issue with using Spirits in plots but I acknowledge that its not to everyones taste and is easy to misuse/use dully.</b><br /> <br /> I've mentioned previously that I know players in my local group that have issues with Spirit plot and that issue is largely due to several Forsaken games they were in before I met them.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I've mentioned previously that MY players in the past have deeply enjoyed the very &quot;dark abstract reflection&quot; take I use when employing the Shadow in a game. So I definitely have an appreciation for the &quot;Silent Hill quality&quot; of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> As a general reply to your last post Christain A I get your point.<br /> <br /> I think the important facet to draw out of your argument is that you are obviously a good ST. Your various 101/1001 plot threads in the forums show you have a natural talent for plot hooks.<br /> <br /> I've never played in a Werewolf game, just to reiterate that point. My soul experience with Werewolf is as an ST using them as very generic quasi-antagonists or set dressing for my worlds. They've never been the focus and they've pretty much universally (with one notable exception) been off screen.<br /> <br /> So all the &quot;player&quot; experience I have is <b>all second hand</b> and I received these accounts about a year after I read the core Forsaken rulebook. So there is a slight disconnect between the book as it is written and the game as it is played. As all my anecdotal evidence is going to be other peoples accounts. Yes, I realize that's a very bad position to be in when it comes to deciding if you like a game. Mainly because those second-hand accounts will taint your view from the start.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned in my opening post, I found the corebook bland so the game did not insta-hook me like say Vampire did. That's a conclusion I came to without any outside influence. Likewise, my base opinion of certain Antagonists such as the Maeljin and Bale Hounds comes from that reading (though to be fair I've read up on the Maeljin more in generic NWoD line books since so they are fresher in my memory). As demonstrated, a lot of whatever I got out of those books has been forgotten or warped by later stimulus.<br /> <br /> When I talk about play-style and usage of said antagonists I mainly have second-hand accounts to go off, with the exception of the Possessed and generic Spirits which I have direct experience with in other game lines (Hunter) as an ST.<br /> <br /> So to finally come back to the &quot;good ST&quot; point I made a while earlier:<br /> <br /> The second hand accounts I have never mentioned even the slightest of the narrative aspects you mentioned. I was talking with this group of players last night, so some of their accounts are pretty fresh in my mind. To detail below:<br /> <br /> Spirits are active, not reactive in nature. They cause problems, problems don't cause them. As such going and hitting the Spirit till its dead (and with the right powers even something as powerful as a spirit can and does die) and that solves the problem (and the plot), because the Spirit was causing the problem. If a Spirit is too powerful do some research (because research can find anything) until you know its ban, repeat above action.<br /> <br /> Hosts are just reskinned spirits that are there for when your characters feel like a &quot;dungeon crawl&quot;. Combat monsters but never anything more complex then that. Janitor duty.<br /> <br /> The Pure are all fanatics who are at least partially insane and have no legitimacy in their philosophy. Sometimes they can be allied with if something even worse shows up.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds worship the Devil(s) and are cultists. Utterly evil and irredeemable, never sympathetic, power hungry fools.<br /> <br /> Humans are a resource, yep, the Forsaken had a pretty dim view of humanity as anything other then &quot;camouflage&quot; and &quot;breeding stock&quot; by most account.<br /> <br /> They never played a plot involving the Idigam so that may be why I have a wider appreciation for them.<br /> <br /> Can you see how what I've been told and what you describe are two completely different games? Same source material, one in the hands of a good ST the other in the hands of a bad ST.<br /> <br /> Maybe Britain has a glut of bad Werewolf ST's ? Because talking to other player groups here usually ends up with similar stories to my local group. Some are better then others.<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I've never seen anyone use or even think of using a Spirit in a &quot;reactive manner&quot; as you mention above Christian A. Even I was using &quot;active&quot; Spirit plot in my Hunter game, but at least I did not make a hash of it.<br /> <br /> The way you talk about interacting with Spirit plot so that it does not become: <i><b>fight it, research it, ritual it</b></i> does sound a lot more interesting then the way I've seen it done in the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113853#post113853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits and the Shadow are one of my favorite bits of Forsaken. It's an entire alien world of symbolism and weirdness that's right next to reality, inhabited with its own thronging society of Broods, Descants and Choirs, spirit courts all plotting against one another and clashing over spreading their favoured Resonance. Spirit totems are a brilliant way to get a pack embroiled in Shadow politics; the rise of one particular totem through the Court of electricity and information was a major source of plot and conflict for the pack in the longest W:tF chronicle I've run.<br /> <br /> There's so much you can do with the Shadow, especially when you delve into the <i>history</i> of an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an alien environment the Shadow is great definitely. If Idigam Chronicles wants to put more emphasis on Spirit Politics I'll not complain. I like a good bit of negotation, wheeling-and-dealing and political maneuvering in a game. Linked to my above points, I think emphasizing the correct time and use of research in regards to Spirits should also be emphasized.<br /> <br /> Nothing worse then having PC's making extended rolls to look up bans in musty old tomes (which is one way I've seen this handled). At the same time having quests into the Shadow and parlaying with Spirits is, while more interesting, also going to run a little dry if you have to do it to find any troublesome spirits ban (though there are always other options of course).<br /> <br /> Then there's Totems, if you have a pack totem that's a Spirit of Knowledge, can't you &quot;selective feed&quot; it other knowledge Spirits? Making it grow in rank and gain power? Given the nature of Spirits would it then inherently have a chance of gaining the possible knowledge of an enemy's weakness e.g. another spirits ban? Or would that knowledge have to be objectively present within one of the Spirits it was fed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:53:17-07:00","id":114150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114138#post114138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all the &quot;player&quot; experience I have is <b>all second hand</b> and I received these accounts about a year after I read the core Forsaken rulebook. So there is a slight disconnect between the book as it is written and the game as it is played. As all my anecdotal evidence is going to be other peoples accounts. Yes, I realize that's a very bad position to be in when it comes to deciding if you like a game. Mainly because those second-hand accounts will taint your view from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>True!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114138#post114138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you see how what I've been told and what you describe are two completely different games? Same source material, one in the hands of a good ST the other in the hands of a bad ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd respectfully disagree, I prefer to think that one of the STs has read the books and the other one hasn't.<br /> <br /> As the corebook quote posted by Satchel has demonstrated, <b>it's all in the books. </b>If you run the antagonists the way you've described, then, in my opinion, you're not running Werewolf: the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The problem is, in my opinion, mainly with people not giving the books a thorough read.<br /> <br /> I really wish your first experiences with Werewolf had been better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 04-16-2014, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:09:51-07:00","id":114162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114150#post114150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the corebook quote posted by Satchel has demonstrated, <b>it's all in the books. </b>If you run the antagonists the way you're described, then, in my opinion, you're not running Werewolf: the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> The problem is, in my opinion, mainly with people not giving the books a thorough read.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, as I've mentioned repeatedly in other threads, the core problem that seems to lead to these oversights is that <b>it's in <i>all</i> the books<i>. </i></b>The line has a distribution-of-data problem, which will hopefully be somewhat remedied with a more consolidated set of relevant information in Idigam, even if it's just in the form of things like general guidelines to portraying spirits in the Storytelling section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:13:48-07:00","id":114165,"title":"","content":"On the relative sympathetic-ness of the Bale Hounds (I enjoy talking about Bale Hounds. I think every Werewolf game should have one of these neat little critters):<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds are people. A Bale Hound is every werewolf, on a bad day.<br /> <br /> You don't join the Bale Hounds by approaching the gods of sin and asking to join up, you join them by being yourself - on a bad day.<br /> <br /> Your grandfather dies. There's grief and there's shock, but there's also rage, rage at the doctors who botched the surgery that should have been a very easy operation, who didn't take the necessary precautions.<br /> <br /> The new girl gets the promotion that you have been promised. It's probably simply because she's more attractive than you.<br /> <br /> Your wife has stopped sleeping with you. She simply doesn't find you attractive any more. She's probably sleeping around.<br /> <br /> Doesn't that make you angry? Doesn't that make you feel wronged? Shouldn't someone pay?<br /> <br /> Add to this the emotional, deeply passionate nature of the Forsaken race. We all have felt really, really angry at one point or another in our lives. When werewolves feel angry, they don't feel like hitting someone the way we do, they feel like transforming into 3 meters of raging wolf-death, tearing someone's throat out and drowning him in his own blood.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hound philosophy isn't scary because it's about alienation from humanity or worship of Outer Evil, it's scary because it's about human vices, human emotions and human feelings gone wrong. What makes the Bale Hounds tragic, sympathetic figures is that their horror is human horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:24:28-07:00","id":114178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114162#post114162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, as I've mentioned repeatedly in other threads, the core problem that seems to lead to these oversights is that <b>it's in <i>all</i> the books<i>. </i></b>The line has a distribution-of-data problem, which will hopefully be somewhat remedied with a more consolidated set of relevant information in Idigam, even if it's just in the form of things like general guidelines to portraying spirits in the Storytelling section.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think a lot of lines have had this problem, and it's one of the reasons I love that they are doing the Chronicle books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:39:27-07:00","id":114187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114162#post114162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, as I've mentioned repeatedly in other threads, the core problem that seems to lead to these oversights is that <b>it's in <i>all</i> the books<i>. </i></b>The line has a distribution-of-data problem, which will hopefully be somewhat remedied with a more consolidated set of relevant information in Idigam, even if it's just in the form of things like general guidelines to portraying spirits in the Storytelling section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some Game lines suffer from this more then others.<br /> <br /> Mage is terrible for it, because its such an expansive game and tries to include a bit of everything. Changeling has it pretty bad as well. Werewolf apparently suffers too. Hell even Giest has issues with it and that's a line made up of 2 books. <br /> <br /> Mummy is a bit of a special case in that its core is very &quot;lite&quot; so its not so much that info is scattered around the books as each book is kinda vital to complete the picture of a fully realized Mummy game. <br /> <br /> Vampire and Promethean are probably the most &quot;condensed&quot; in terms of their material I think. They have everything they need and all their key points are adequately emphasized in the core book. Demon too comes pretty close, with a few missing items (Demonic Children, Suborned infrastructure). <br /> <br /> Anyway, before we got neck deep into the common misconceptions about Forsaken and a bucket load of bad-campaign reports on my side we were talking a bit more generally about what makes Werewolf work as a game. <br /> <br /> I've noticed we've gone and focused on a thread of negativity in the last couple pages. While its good to examine criticism of the game and think about them, I was really more interested in peoples positive experiences with the game line when I made this thread. Some posters have been pretty awesome at teasing out aspects and stories I would have never thought of myself and that's been fun and interesting. Others have tried framing the themes of the game under different lights for me, which has been an interesting thought experiment in and of itself. <br /> <br /> I think I want to steer the thread a little bit more towards the Idigam Chronicle stuff. We've only got basic teasers so far, so all we can do is speculate as to what the book and therefore new edition of the game is going to be like in its final presentation.<br /> <br /> Still what are people looking forward to the most about the Chronicle book?<br /> <br /> Charlaquin has mentioned previously, for example, that he/she is looking forward to being able to emphasis the more traditional Werewolf tropes of being &quot;at war with yourself&quot; or feeling &quot;ill suited to your own skin&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:06:38-07:00","id":114201,"title":"","content":"She. Indeed, I'm glad to see those themes getting a bit more attention in Wolf Blooded and Harmony. Can't wait to see the Kuruth preview as well. It's really nice to see there will be super classic Lon Chaney style werewolves in the form of Wolf Blooded with Dalu form and Death Rage, as well as more modern takes like Red from Once Upon a Time with Urhan form and being forced to shift at their Auspice moon. I'm really happy that Harmony starting out as &quot;too human&quot; at high levels and making it easier to Death Rage and harder to willingly shape-shift, sliding down to &quot;Balanced&quot;, and then having the opposite extreme of &quot;too spirit&quot; on the other end making it hard not to shape-shift at awkward times and adding spirit banes is like my ideal version of the Werewolf's inner struggle. But most importantly, I'm happy that the new Harmony finally gives characters who don't want to be Werewolves and instinctively fight their nature a tangible reason to WANT to start doing Uratha things. I always found it weird that I was just supposed to accept &quot;you're a Werewolf now. Come fight spirits and stuff with us! Join one of these Tribes with codes that are alien to your human morality!&quot; I'll admit that particular experience had more to do with having a terrible ST than any inherent fault of Werewolf. But I love that now the established Uratha can come to newly-first-changed Werewolves and tell them &quot;We know how you feel. Join our pack and we can teach you to control it.&quot; And that will actually be reflected in the game mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:13:32-07:00","id":114205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114201#post114201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Join one of these Tribes with codes that are alien to your human morality!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>:/<br /> <br /> Hmmmmmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:35:38-07:00","id":114217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114205#post114205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> :/ Hmmmmmm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wow, you took totally the wrong thing away from that post. Did you miss the part immediately after where I said &quot;that had more to do with having a terrible ST than any actual flaw of Werewolf&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:37:15-07:00","id":114218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114217#post114217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wow, you took totally the wrong thing away from that post. Did you miss the part immediately after where I said &quot;that had more to do with having a terrible ST than any actual flaw of Werewolf&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't - it's just that I've seen this perspective stated as a fact by other people all too often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:40:32-07:00","id":114221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114218#post114218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't - it's just that I've seen this perspective stated as a fact by other people all too often.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, that's really not how the tribes are meant to be portrayed, but it is an all too common misconception. A bad or even just misinformed ST can really ruin a new player's perceptions of what Forsaken is actually like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:55:31-07:00","id":114231,"title":"","content":"Want an exemple of a good campaign ? Read this <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?446663-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-quot-Detroit-Rock-City-quot\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...Rock-City-quot</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:59:53-07:00","id":114234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114221#post114221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, that's really not how the tribes are meant to be portrayed, but it is an all too common misconception. A bad or even just misinformed ST can really ruin a new player's perceptions of what Forsaken is actually like.</div> </div> </div> </div> On a related note, I love that tribes are getting a bit more focus. I assume the tribal bans will remain the same (in fact, I hope they do), but it'll be nice having a distinct culture for each Tribe that arises around the prey that they consider most dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T12:24:20-07:00","id":114248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114201#post114201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She. Indeed, I'm glad to see those themes getting a bit more attention in Wolf Blooded and Harmony. Can't wait to see the Kuruth preview as well. It's really nice to see there will be super classic Lon Chaney style werewolves in the form of Wolf Blooded with Dalu form and Death Rage, as well as more modern takes like Red from Once Upon a Time with Urhan form and being forced to shift at their Auspice moon. I'm really happy that Harmony starting out as &quot;too human&quot; at high levels and making it easier to Death Rage and harder to willingly shape-shift, sliding down to &quot;Balanced&quot;, and then having the opposite extreme of &quot;too spirit&quot; on the other end making it hard not to shape-shift at awkward times and adding spirit banes is like my ideal version of the Werewolf's inner struggle. But most importantly, I'm happy that the new Harmony finally gives characters who don't want to be Werewolves and instinctively fight their nature a tangible reason to WANT to start doing Uratha things. I always found it weird that I was just supposed to accept &quot;you're a Werewolf now. Come fight spirits and stuff with us! Join one of these Tribes with codes that are alien to your human morality!&quot; I'll admit that particular experience had more to do with having a terrible ST than any inherent fault of Werewolf. But I love that now the established Uratha can come to newly-first-changed Werewolves and tell them &quot;We know how you feel. Join our pack and we can teach you to control it.&quot; And that will actually be reflected in the game mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree with this totally. This was one of little problems I had with <b>Forsaken</b> before, but now I could incorporate it in to play.<br /> <br /> I could be count as sucess stories of this topic, as I really would like to run <b>Werewolf</b> game with Bale Hounds and proper run Shadow Realm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-16-2014, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T12:33:05-07:00","id":114253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114201#post114201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Join one of these Tribes with codes that are alien to your human morality!</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, so I guess it was just me that felt it already made sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T12:46:10-07:00","id":114263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114253#post114253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Huh, so I guess it was just me that felt it already made sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, you're missing the point of my post. I was not expressing my current feelings on Tribes, I was sharing an experience I had with a poor ST in my first Forsaken game. Fortunately I have since realized that this is not the intent, but my experience does not seem to be uncommon among new Werewolf players. As such, I am glad the approach to tribes is being brushed up a bit. It will help avoid this confusion for future newcomers, so they don't have to have the same bad first impression I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T14:59:25-07:00","id":114349,"title":"","content":"To be fair to Charlaquin, a lot of players I know had issue with the old Harmony system and Werewolf culture in general. <br /> <br /> Once again, need to frame this as the fact that they've had terrible experiences with the game thanks to a terrible ST. So they are not inclined to look favorably on the game.<br /> <br /> They take issue with the idea that after the first change its kinda like <b>BAM!</b> your on Harmony now, not Morality. Just by dint of you gaining this template you suddenly don't have to play by Human morals anymore. Also some things that would have been inconsequential to you an hour before your first change are now big deals! Oh and you except all this out of hand, because you know Spiritual enlightenment of your true destiny or whatever. <br /> <br /> Basically they would prefer a Harmony system that shows a persons gradual &quot;slip&quot; into the Werewolf mindset that is reinforced by a culture that has an objective &quot;right&quot; view on how all this Werewolf stuff works. Luckily, the new version of Harmony seems to do this so I'm pretty sure even a group as &quot;damaged&quot; towards Forsaken as my local one could give Idigam another chance.<br /> <br /> As for Tribal bans and such, I kinda hope Idigam takes a page from Demon and has them be &quot;Tribe Conditions&quot; that give you a positive effect in regards to the your specialist type of prey but give you a negative effect as well. <br /> <br /> In general, I think it can be said from the accounts of a few different people on this thread that a good portion of people who are ST Forsaken seem to have got the wrong end of the stick when running it. Alternatively one could say they've placed the emphasis of the game in the wrong place. Which might have something to do with the phenomenon that Satchel pointed out previously about the way information is presented in the Werewolf books. <br /> <br /> I honestly can't say how common this phenomenon is in general. All I can speak for is my local group of roleplayers and a couple of other groups I've met at conventions here in the UK. Still it seems to be more common over here with Forsaken then say Requiem or Changeling. Which is kinda odd. Also very unfortunate for the game line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T15:29:55-07:00","id":114365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114218#post114218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't - it's just that I've seen this perspective stated as a fact by other people all too often.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be right and it might be wrong but it does come up quite a bit. Without tediously making rather large setting riffs all the time a lot of people I play with would rather be ghost wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T16:15:00-07:00","id":114390,"title":"","content":"Presumably a more concisely written book would help with storytellers not getting it right.<br /> <br /> That said, my first game of Werewolf had us in a city mostly populated by the Pure, who were living sort of undercover. Everyone thought everyone in the city was Forsaken, but they were, by a vast majority, Pure. So you didn't know what packs you could trust. It was a very good game, even knowing what I know now, and we had a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> Now, the Pure book makes it clear that that isn't likely. Pure are identified by the ruined scars where their brands to Luna were torn from them. Certainly there's quislings, people who have moved over to the faith of the Pure but still exist among the Forsaken to feed them up to their enemies, but most times you're going to be able to readily identify a Pure just on sight, or when you hear them talk about how they're going to kill you. The thing is, the Pure book didn't come out for a long while after the corebook came out (over a year), and even then you might not have bought it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T22:26:47-07:00","id":114556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114390#post114390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the Pure book makes it clear that that isn't likely. Pure are identified by the ruined scars where their brands to Luna were torn from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, you only get to see spirit brands and the scars of the Pure in the Shadow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T06:19:30-07:00","id":114680,"title":"","content":"First, my apologies for taking so long to reply. I ended up more than a little busy, unexpectedly. That said, some replies. :-)<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, a disclaimer: this is all my personal opinion ONLY. Do not consider anything I say here as a spoiler for the book, nor is it necessarily how the book is written. I am only one person out of an entire team working on the thing, and I'm certainly not the developer. Further, I'm speaking from the point of view of the game as it is now, not the book coming out. It wouldn't be fair for me to use information in the discussion that I can't expect others to have. Just keep that all in mind, please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be presumptive on my part (well maybe a little) but wyrdhamster has already mentioned previously in the thread that he is not a huge fan of the Shadow and its inherent animistic nature. I suspect his issue with Forsaken is that the majority of its antagonists find their home/origin/nature defined to some extent by the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand not liking something; that said, with as much as Forsaken tends to interact with the Shadow as a default, the base game probably just isn't to those folks' taste. I don't say that as a bad thing, nor as some sort of silly &quot;find another game to play&quot; scenario either. It simply is what it is. I don't care for seafood; as such, I tend to not set foot in Red Lobster. Now, I have, because they do have steak and I can eat that (although it still had a bit of a fishy taste to me), but it's not the default assumption of going to Red Lobster for dinner. Similarly, if one does not like spirits or the Shadow, then the default game of Forsaken as currently presented requires some massaging to get it to one's tastes.<br /> <br /> Now, I think that The Idigam Chronicle makes it a bit easier to do that than the previous core book, but then again I'm biased, so take that as you will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can voice my thoughts on the antagonists within the Forsaken gameline with a little more confidence however, I'm kinda fascinated to here a writers thoughts on these same issues so yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that I necessarily have any greater insight into things other than the fact that I've played and run Forsaken since it came out. Actually, before it came out - I was lucky enough to win a seat in the Golden Ticket LARP 2005 (I was part of the Camarilla at the time, and that was a potential reward for recruiting new members. Bit of a story to explain, I guess.). Regardless, as part of that event, I got to play in a game of Forsaken run by a White Wolf staffer at the time, and we got a bunch of swag. But I don't think my opinion &quot;as a writer&quot; has any more weight on its own merit than someone else's, you know? Everyone's opinion is valued; some merely have more material to work from. It's not like the difference between, say, someone who's a high school science student and Neil Degrasse Tyson. :-)<br /> <br /> Before commenting on individual antagonists/prey, I'll say one thing that governs all of them: you get out of your antagonists what you put into them. In my opinion, that's true of gaming as a whole, but from the ST's perspective, I find that interesting and well thought-out antagonists help drive the story. If your antagonists are flat, one-note villains, then that's all you're going to get out of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Form what I remember (considering I have not read a Forsaken book since about 2010) their Antagonists roughly are:<br /> <br /> <b>Other Werewolves:</b> Divided into: The Pure, Bale Hounds and rival Forsaken Packs your PC's have issues/history with.</div> </div> </div> </div>All potentially true. I think these guys provide interesting moral issues. Imru Nu Fir Imru, after all - the People Must Not Murder the People. The characters may certainly choose to kill other werewolves if they like, but it is not only against their own laws, but they also have to check against their Harmony. Plus, the Pure provide a dilemma themselves - from the outside, they appear to have more than the Forsaken. The spirits don't hate them, their packs are bigger, they have more territory, etc. It's only when a werewolf changes sides, thinking the grass is greener, that they find out the truth on the inside, that the Pure are a terrifying cult basically. I tend to play the Pure as a &quot;there but for the grace of Luna go I&quot; antagonist.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds I've already shared my opinion on I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spirits:</b> Divided into: Mageth, inherently &quot;negative&quot; spirits of concepts such as murder, rape etc. Arguably any spirit that screws with stuff on the wrong side of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wouldn't separate spirits into categories. First, they don't necessarily fit neatly into any taxonomy. Second, I like screwing with my players' heads. I helped run a plot in the local Cam game wherein the plot took place in an amusement park within our domain borders. What was happening was that people were having heart attacks or other physical ailments when riding a number of thrill rides in the park - roller coasters and such - and a few had died. One might think the roller coaster spirits had something to do with it, or some &quot;negative&quot; spirit, but no. Spirits of joy were simply using their Influences to make people have even more fun, which sometimes translated into serious health issues when combined with adrenaline on the thrill rides. Taking something most folks see as &quot;good&quot; and flipping it into an antagonist was interesting, and the players were noticeably shocked when they found out what was going on. It was a good time. :-)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spirit Hosts:</b> Divided into: Urged or Claimed</div> </div> </div> </div>I've used the Claimed more often than the Urged, I think. Even so, I honestly rarely use them unless the story is going that way. That's just personal preference though I think. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shards:</b> Spider, Rat, Raven, Locust, Mushroom, Snake, Wolf? (Not sure about that last one, also sure I am missing some)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Adarasharu (the Wolf Hosts) showed up in Night Horrors: Wolfsbane, so you're right there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Maeljin:</b> Divided into: Maelinet and Maelin I believe. If your using Inferno then the &quot;possessed&quot; from that book might come under this group as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maeltinet are servants or avatars of a sort of the Maeljin, yes. And sure, I could agree with putting the Possessed in that category, dependent upon how one views the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Idigam:</b> Can't speak to any changes in the new book, but to my understanding at current they are primordial spirits with no reflective aspect in the material world, making them &quot;impossible&quot; my normal spirits standards. May or may not embody the every idea of &quot;change&quot; or &quot;evolution&quot; in some regards, subject to debate. All are monstrously powerful and basically impossible to permanently kill, above and beyond even normal spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are certainly very tough to kill, yes. You basically nailed these guys. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of those 6 categories all but Other Werewolves (and even they involve Spirits (Pack Totems) and the Shadow (using it in warfare) by their nature) are basically spirits in one fashion or another. Just to tie this back to issues wyrdhamster might have for a second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, although honestly I see the Hosts - or at least the two default ones, as the game doesn't assume a Storyteller is using any more than those - more as physical antagonists. Sure, they interact with the hisil, but most things in Forsaken do because that's the game. Again, the game is just a toolkit and it can be played without the Shadow, but the default assumes it.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd respectfully submit that you've omitted an antagonist. And that's okay because it seems most folks don't count humans as a viable antagonist for werewolves. And certainly, in a face-to-face fight? A human is going to get pasted in short order. So don't use them that way. Use them in oblique ways. Maybe part of the pack's territory is being rezoned by someone in city council. Is it on purpose? Does he know about the werewolves? Or is it just an accident that the territory's resonance is going to change, and new spirits will be created while old ones may die (thus shifting the spirit politics around, and maybe destroying one of the pack's spirit allies)? How does the pack deal with the problem - they can't just walk into a city council meeting, shift into Gauru and unleash hell. Well, okay, they can I guess, but boy does that create more problems than it solves.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll revitalize my blog at some point and do little advice columns on the various antagonists. That's a thought.<br /> <br /> Hmm....this is getting very long. I think I'll cut this here and do the rest in a second part, just to not hit the character limit. (Hopefully.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T06:37:54-07:00","id":114687,"title":"","content":"Okay, continuing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the rival pack thing because its very Human and no one is out-and-out the bad guy. Its basically like watching to human gangs go to war in something like The Wire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, although personally, I try my best (with differing levels of success) to make sure nobody is an out-and-out bad guy. But then, I like painting with various shades of grey in my games when I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure never did anything for me, fanatical extremist Werewolves that believe in a return to a more primitive world where they are the top-dogs is a little 1-note for me. They remind me just a little bit to much of some of the 2nd Ed Masquerade stuff on the Sabbat, before they got fleshed out to be a more complex socio-religious apocalypse cult/church of Caine. I can't even put my finger on what I feel is lacking about them, only that they feel slightly redundant to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, although have you read <b>The Pure</b>? That book got me thinking about the Anshega in a different light and opened up new story ideas for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bale Hounds, well I've already talked on this issue a bit in this thread. Thought later posters comments have got me thinking about them in more Faust/Dorian Grey aesthetics that I can dig. So I guess I could say I like them as complex self-involved villains and not cackling infernalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a WoD game, I've yet to see a time where a cackling infernalist is a good idea. That may just be me and my tastes, but still. I like some complex villains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits, kinda already made my supposition here. Either you enjoy Spirit plot or you don't. I don't have a huge issue with it, I know people that do. Only so many times you can play the twenty questions game of &quot;what sort of spirit is it&quot; and &quot;what are its bans and how do we find them&quot; etc. I find making my Shadow more like the other world of the Silent Hill games and its denizens about a similar sorta tone is enough that the creepy aesthetics and atmosphere is enough to keep players engaged for the most part (at least in the context of Hunter and Mage, never run Werewolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to play up the spirit politics angle. It's hard sometimes, because spirits have motivations that don't necessarily correspond ours, but I try to make it interesting and a bit alien. In the past, I gave one character a Pyromania Derangement (although man am I glad we're moving away from Derangements) after making a deal with a fire-spirit. Another character found a minor time spirit to ask it a question, and made the mistake of starting the conversation with &quot;May I speak with you a minute?&quot; to which I responded in-character, &quot;Sure. You have one minute. Go.&quot; The look on that player's face was priceless. I then got the &quot;You know, I should have frelling knew better than to put things that way&quot; comment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit Hosts add a human element that can be interesting and throw up moral dilemmas for sure. Particularly because possession can make a plot deeply personal I feel. Ran a possession plot as part of a Hunter Campaign and it was the plot that I got the most positive feedback from my players on. I think it grounds or internalized Spirit plot which can otherwise be very, very external in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since your next section is Shards, I'm assuming you mean the Urged/Claimed here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, that is exactly what I've used them to do, to hit players on a personal level. Loss of control is a terrifying thing, as is hopelessness. Putting those into a story (in a respectful measure of course - it's too easy to go overboard) can really lend it gravity and make the story interesting and cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shards are creepy and other and have a slightly different feel from your default Spirit Antagonists, but they are a &quot;known&quot; threat a lot of the time. The People know how to deal with them, what they do and where they come from. I've seen game where clearing out the Rat and Spider nests is almost treated like janitor duty by the PC's because its just seen as &quot;a job&quot; inhered from Father Wolf and with little real feeling of feel (though a healthy respect for the danger involved).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, both Hosts directly do bad things to a territory. In the case of an Azlu infestation, as the Shadow is cut off from the physical by a strengthened Gauntlet, folks start to become, well, less alive. The thickened Gauntlet can lead to Shoals and the like, causing depression and so on, dragging down the whole territory if not stopped. The Beshilu bring with them a whole host of problems, from spirit invasion more likely, to more disease-spirits and the like. When I use these antagonists, I try to make things more personal. Things are happening in the character's turf right now. This isn't because your great great great (keep that going for a while, I'm not typing it out) grandfather didn't get the job done. It's because monsters are messing with what's yours. Tonight. Are you going to do something about it, or are you going to roll over and take it?<br /> <br /> I find that some degree of urgency coupled with affecting things directly helps give an antagonist some &quot;punch,&quot; if you will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maeljin I've already shared my thoughts about. I think they are a bit of an ill fit and feel slightly bolted on to the setting (bit like the Pure actually). I liked the that later books in the NWoD game line kinda explained them more (Inferno) and I'm even happy to include some of the Mage fluff on them (Summoners/Imperial Mysteries). So I guess coming at them from mainly either a core NWoD viewpoint or a Hunter/Mage viewpoint they look a bit odd/off in Werewolf, despite it being the game that introduced them. Let me put it this way, in my games I consider it cannon that the Maeljin and their ephemeral servants are NOT actually Spirits but demons/denizens of a realm within the lower depths.<br /> <br /> I think I'd like them to be refluffed to be more &quot;equal opportunity&quot; bad guys. So instead of just showing up in the Wounds in the Shadow they have a presence in the Astral, Hedge and Underworld that way the game lines that interact with those realms each get a piece of the puzzle in regards to the Maeljin/Archdukes of the Inferno/Denizens of the Lower Depths from their particular supernatural races viewpoint. Still, have said supernaturals be at least a little genre savvy e.g. Werewolves realize that Maeljin stuff is not actually Spirit related, more a case of something &quot;other&quot; intruding into the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know what the plan is for the Maeljin going forward. Not really my department at present (although, like I said, if we do a Bale Hounds book, I'd love to work on it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=113744#post113744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam I actually like as an idea. Werewolf I think needed a grounded &quot;big bad&quot; that could be held up as such. Requiem likewise needed something similar and the Strix provide that roll really well. I have issue with some of the fluff around them (mutant babies? thrown to the moon? moon landings?) as its a bit weird. The core idea of Spirits that &quot;should not be&quot; and &quot;don't play by the rules&quot; and represent ideas so abstract and primordial then sentient life can't really grasp onto them without going kinda nuts. It gives something that is definitively &quot;other&quot; in a game that is already kinda full of a sense of the &quot;other&quot;.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, I'm dying to see what the writers come up with for them in the new book, if they get the same sort of extra development and thematic shot in the arm that the Strix did in Blood and Smoke I'd be tempted to use them as major villains in any game line in the NWoD (save maybe Vampire and Mummy).<br /> <br /> \u200bThis reply got out of hand, was supposed to be shorter then this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hopefully you like the idigam in the new book. I think they're interesting and will hopefully prove to be useful and terrifying antagonists for folks' games. But then, I'm a bit biased in that regard. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T06:40:44-07:00","id":114688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114218#post114218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't - it's just that I've seen this perspective stated as a fact by other people all too often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if I may: if you've seen it all too often, that probably says something. To wit, it means that we need to be clearer about things in The Idigam Chronicle and not scatter needed information over several books. Within reason, of course - if we'd put everything into one book, it might be the size of one of those 20th Anniversary Edition books!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T08:44:19-07:00","id":114731,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that very extensive reply Strider1276.<br /> <br /> Always awesome when one of the writers/devs comes in and chats about this stuff with the fans.<br /> <br /> I think most posters in the thread agree about the clarity and distribution of information in regard to Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I read the core years ago and then skimmed read a couple of the splats and half the thematic stuff and themes and such I just plain missed. Later second-hand stuff also kinda screwed up my perception of a lot of the games tone and ideas.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think Idigam Chronicles definitely would benefit from a slightly later &quot;ST Chapter&quot; then Blood and Smoke did. Just a couple of pages on the proper/good use of Spirits would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T09:26:51-07:00","id":114744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click?p=114688#post114688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if I may: 